1235
01:05:36,042 --> 01:05:39,125
<i>As our Lord was, I am betrayed by Judas.</i>

1236
01:05:39,667 --> 01:05:41,500
Gentlemen, may I have a moment?

1237
01:05:42,250 --> 01:05:44,250
(Wicks) <i>Judas in many forms.</i>

1238
01:05:44,333 --> 01:05:45,917
(melancholic music plays)

1239
01:05:46,000 --> 01:05:48,833
<i>Always the true threat comes from within.</i>

1240
01:05:50,292 --> 01:05:52,125
<i>Remember my words.</i>

1241
01:05:53,583 --> 01:05:56,958
<i>On this Good Friday,
remember what's to come.</i>

1242
01:05:57,042 --> 01:05:59,042
<i>Remember, all of you.</i>

1243
01:06:00,667 --> 01:06:02,958
(Martha crying) You will rise again.

1244
01:06:04,125 --> 01:06:05,542
It will be okay.

1245
01:06:06,042 --> 01:06:07,667
You will rise again.

1246
01:06:08,292 --> 01:06:09,500
You will rise.

1247
01:06:09,583 --> 01:06:12,958
(Wicks) <i>The hour approaches.</i>
<i>The hour I have warned you about.</i>

1248
01:06:14,542 --> 01:06:17,542
<i>Remember what I have promised you all,
come Easter Sunday.</i>

1249
01:06:17,625 --> 01:06:21,458
For I will make good
on that promise, yes, I will.

1250
01:06:21,542 --> 01:06:23,417
(dramatic music plays)

1251
01:06:23,500 --> 01:06:25,708
(Wicks) <i>For behold,</i>
<i>though He is struck down,</i>

1252
01:06:25,792 --> 01:06:29,125
<i>the righteous Son of God will rise again.</i>

1253
01:06:29,667 --> 01:06:32,083
<i>Eve's Apple restored to the tree</i>

1254
01:06:32,167 --> 01:06:35,833
<i>and the wealth of His kingdom
and His rising reign.</i>

1255
01:06:36,458 --> 01:06:39,292
<i>And as you gnash your teeth
in the darkness,</i>

1256
01:06:39,375 --> 01:06:41,000
<i>you unfaithful devils,</i>

1257
01:06:41,083 --> 01:06:45,500
<i>as you lie cold and forgotten and alone,</i>

1258
01:06:45,583 --> 01:06:50,000
He will rise again to reclaim what is His.

1259
01:06:50,667 --> 01:06:52,292
And strike down the wicked

1260
01:06:53,042 --> 01:06:56,083
and raise His true Son
to the throne of this nation!

1261
01:06:56,167 --> 01:06:59,375
Yes, He will rise! Yes, He will rise!

1262
01:06:59,458 --> 01:07:02,083
Yes, tremble in fear,

1263
01:07:02,167 --> 01:07:07,667
for He will rise again in glory
and vengeance and power!

1264
01:07:07,750 --> 01:07:09,667
- (music fades)
- (machine whirs, hisses)

1265
01:07:14,208 --> 01:07:15,958
(forklift beeping)

1266
01:07:17,542 --> 01:07:20,792
Sorry about your loss, Father.
Here, sign on the bottom. (Clears throat)

1267
01:07:21,667 --> 01:07:23,042
Listen, between you and me,

1268
01:07:23,125 --> 01:07:26,458
I don't care what the Internet says.
I think there's a chance you didn't do it.

1269
01:07:26,542 --> 01:07:27,542
(pats back)

1270
01:07:29,667 --> 01:07:31,875
All right, everyone. Listen up.

1271
01:07:31,958 --> 01:07:34,208
Oh, would you look who it is.
It's Judas Jud.

1272
01:07:34,292 --> 01:07:37,167
- (scoffs)
- Father, you are not welcome here.

1273
01:07:37,250 --> 01:07:38,458
All right, stop!

1274
01:07:38,542 --> 01:07:39,750
Here's what's gonna happen.

1275
01:07:39,833 --> 01:07:42,417
Benoit fricken' Blanc and I are
gonna ask you all some questions,

1276
01:07:42,500 --> 01:07:45,667
you'll answer them and we'll get to
the bottom of who killed Monsignor Wicks

1277
01:07:45,750 --> 01:07:48,000
and why and then…

1278
01:07:48,792 --> 01:07:50,208
That's it!

1279
01:07:50,292 --> 01:07:53,125
Okay? Okay, so…

1280
01:07:54,917 --> 01:07:57,042
Thank you, Father Jud, that was

1281
01:07:57,125 --> 01:07:58,292
very good. Um,

1282
01:07:58,375 --> 01:08:00,000
and we're gonna start… (sighs)

1283
01:08:00,083 --> 01:08:04,167
…with what happened that night
right here in this very room.

1284
01:08:04,250 --> 01:08:07,292
You mean the time Jud admitted
to all of us that he killed a man.

1285
01:08:07,375 --> 01:08:10,417
Okay, no, that was…
That was the boxing thing, I was...

1286
01:08:10,500 --> 01:08:13,458
And now he's covering his ass
by attacking us. He's a PINO.

1287
01:08:13,542 --> 01:08:14,542
A… a PINO?

1288
01:08:14,583 --> 01:08:16,167
Priest in name only.

1289
01:08:16,250 --> 01:08:20,375
Helping Benoit Blanc
crack the mystery of the evil, evil church

1290
01:08:20,458 --> 01:08:23,708
and then some libtard
will make a podcast about all of this

1291
01:08:23,792 --> 01:08:27,708
and before you know it, the idiot versions
of all of us will end up on Netflix.

1292
01:08:27,792 --> 01:08:30,500
Oh, the idiot versions. God forbid.

1293
01:08:30,583 --> 01:08:31,833
(screams)

1294
01:08:31,917 --> 01:08:33,292
- (shrieks)
- (Nat) Jesus!

1295
01:08:33,375 --> 01:08:34,792
It's a miracle!

1296
01:08:36,042 --> 01:08:38,917
- I can walk, Martha. It just hurts.
- (exhaling) Oh.

1297
01:08:39,958 --> 01:08:41,875
- (sighs) Oh.
- And I say, good.

1298
01:08:42,542 --> 01:08:43,750
Expose it all.

1299
01:08:44,292 --> 01:08:46,042
Wicks was a con man.

1300
01:08:46,792 --> 01:08:50,208
Miracles and supernatural
power of God bullshit.

1301
01:08:50,792 --> 01:08:53,000
(scoffs) I really believed.

1302
01:08:54,875 --> 01:08:56,500
I still wanna believe.

1303
01:08:56,583 --> 01:08:58,292
(scoffs) How sick is that?

1304
01:08:58,792 --> 01:09:03,042
Well, actually, I was inquiring
not about Jud's prayer group,

1305
01:09:03,125 --> 01:09:05,542
but about the shadowy meeting with Wicks

1306
01:09:05,625 --> 01:09:08,625
that took place in this room
on Palm Sunday.

1307
01:09:09,833 --> 01:09:10,833
(imperceptible)

1308
01:09:10,917 --> 01:09:12,875
(suspenseful sting plays)

1309
01:09:12,958 --> 01:09:16,417
(Benoit) What was
that meeting actually about?

1310
01:09:18,458 --> 01:09:20,292
Who wants to go first?

1311
01:09:21,625 --> 01:09:22,833
I'll tell you.

1312
01:09:26,042 --> 01:09:29,083
- (Nat) Cy. Hey. Wait, hold on, buddy. Hey!
- (Lee) No, no, no.

1313
01:09:29,167 --> 01:09:30,917
You shut your mouth,
you little shit weasel.

1314
01:09:31,000 --> 01:09:32,708
- It isn't your decision!
- Tell him nothing!

1315
01:09:32,792 --> 01:09:34,542
Hey, look… Whoa. Easy, Father Jud.

1316
01:09:34,625 --> 01:09:36,625
I promise you that
what we talked about that night

1317
01:09:36,708 --> 01:09:39,208
has nothing to do
with Wicks' killing, okay?

1318
01:09:39,292 --> 01:09:42,083
But it does have to do with things that,
if made public,

1319
01:09:42,167 --> 01:09:43,625
could ruin people in this room.

1320
01:09:43,708 --> 01:09:46,333
I recorded the whole thing. Just hit play.

1321
01:09:48,875 --> 01:09:50,875
- (Martha) No! This is not...
- (Lee) You scoundrel!

1322
01:09:50,958 --> 01:09:54,417
- Open this door, you bastard!
- You are defiling my files!

1323
01:09:54,500 --> 01:09:56,250
- Play it.
- (Lee) Open it...

1324
01:09:56,333 --> 01:09:58,125
(clock ticking)

1325
01:10:03,917 --> 01:10:05,125
(footsteps approaching)

1326
01:10:07,000 --> 01:10:09,417
(Wicks) All right. Very dramatic, Vera.

1327
01:10:10,417 --> 01:10:12,500
You've got your audience.
What's this about?

1328
01:10:16,208 --> 01:10:18,417
I've been thinking about your mom.

1329
01:10:19,875 --> 01:10:24,792
I never knew her,
but growing up in this church,

1330
01:10:24,875 --> 01:10:28,083
I knew the story of the harlot whore

1331
01:10:28,167 --> 01:10:31,583
and I've been thinking about
what her life must have been like

1332
01:10:31,667 --> 01:10:35,625
to be trapped in a house,
with her father and her son.

1333
01:10:36,458 --> 01:10:39,625
Closing rank, shaming her

1334
01:10:39,708 --> 01:10:42,125
and teaching us all to shame her.

1335
01:10:44,000 --> 01:10:45,417
That poor girl.

1336
01:10:49,792 --> 01:10:51,708
(clicks tongue, inhales)

1337
01:10:51,792 --> 01:10:56,625
Yesterday, I got a call
from a family law colleague in Brooklyn.

1338
01:10:57,375 --> 01:11:00,583
(smacks lips) He wanted to
double-check contact details

1339
01:11:00,667 --> 01:11:04,375
for Monsignor Jefferson Wicks, my client,

1340
01:11:04,458 --> 01:11:08,542
because my client
had filed an AOP with him.

1341
01:11:09,500 --> 01:11:10,708
In Brooklyn.

1342
01:11:11,458 --> 01:11:13,667
So I would not know.

1343
01:11:14,708 --> 01:11:16,250
What's an AOP?

1344
01:11:19,625 --> 01:11:22,042
"Acknowledgement of parentage"?

1345
01:11:25,375 --> 01:11:28,167
"Affirmation that I, Jefferson Wicks,

1346
01:11:28,250 --> 01:11:31,625
am the biological father of Cyrus Draven."

1347
01:11:36,667 --> 01:11:39,083
(Vera) No shame for you.

1348
01:11:40,125 --> 01:11:42,042
Right? (Scoffs)

1349
01:11:42,125 --> 01:11:43,667
Who was the mother?

1350
01:11:45,208 --> 01:11:46,833
Does it even matter?

1351
01:11:47,458 --> 01:11:53,292
No. No! (Scoffs) No, she came back
and dropped this poor kid in your lap.

1352
01:11:53,917 --> 01:11:56,250
And then she went and had a life.

1353
01:11:56,333 --> 01:11:59,833
And my faithful father came to the rescue.

1354
01:11:59,917 --> 01:12:04,250
Once again, the boys club closed ranks
and there I was, the loyal little idiot.

1355
01:12:04,333 --> 01:12:05,542
Trapped.

1356
01:12:05,625 --> 01:12:10,875
And I obeyed
and I honored and raised <i>your </i>son

1357
01:12:10,958 --> 01:12:14,042
while you sat on your pulpit, shameless.

1358
01:12:14,125 --> 01:12:17,917
You… hypocritical son of a bitch!

1359
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:20,292
(breathing heavily)

1360
01:12:21,583 --> 01:12:22,917
(Wicks exhales softly)

1361
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:24,083
(Nat) Cy?

1362
01:12:24,708 --> 01:12:25,708
Did you know?

1363
01:12:25,792 --> 01:12:27,792
Not until Vera told me this morning.

1364
01:12:28,458 --> 01:12:29,458
(Wicks) Yes.

1365
01:12:30,292 --> 01:12:31,917
Cy is my son.

1366
01:12:34,625 --> 01:12:36,458
From a loose woman of no importance

1367
01:12:36,542 --> 01:12:39,333
who I knew for one night
and haven't seen in 30 years.

1368
01:12:39,417 --> 01:12:42,417
Vera's father and I kept this secret.
But no longer.

1369
01:12:42,958 --> 01:12:44,625
He is my heir.

1370
01:12:46,042 --> 01:12:47,125
My son.

1371
01:12:49,625 --> 01:12:51,750
Now the world is going to know it.

1372
01:12:53,208 --> 01:12:55,417
So, rats,

1373
01:12:56,500 --> 01:12:57,792
flee the sinking ship.

1374
01:13:00,250 --> 01:13:01,083
(Nat clears throat)

1375
01:13:01,167 --> 01:13:02,625
Oh, cut the shit.

1376
01:13:02,708 --> 01:13:04,500
You're all standing by your man.

1377
01:13:04,583 --> 01:13:07,875
(scoffs) I just wanted to see it.
I wanted to see for myself.

1378
01:13:07,958 --> 01:13:10,875
You eat his shit with a spoon
and come back for seconds.

1379
01:13:10,958 --> 01:13:12,750
(Lee) That's kind of condescending, Vera.

1380
01:13:12,833 --> 01:13:14,792
- You don't know what we're feeling.
- (scoffs) Oh.

1381
01:13:14,875 --> 01:13:18,917
I think we're all, as Christians,
very shaken up by what you just said.

1382
01:13:20,917 --> 01:13:23,625
But we're fighting an existential war here

1383
01:13:23,708 --> 01:13:25,750
where the end justifies the means.

1384
01:13:25,833 --> 01:13:27,667
The church doesn't need
some pussy who's gonna

1385
01:13:27,750 --> 01:13:29,792
lie down and take it, we need a warrior.

1386
01:13:29,875 --> 01:13:31,500
We need a warrior

1387
01:13:31,583 --> 01:13:35,667
and I believe that God chose
Monsignor Wicks to be His warrior.

1388
01:13:36,417 --> 01:13:39,250
So, you and your son have my sword.

1389
01:13:39,958 --> 01:13:41,000
And…

1390
01:13:42,083 --> 01:13:43,708
We don't know this woman.

1391
01:13:44,708 --> 01:13:46,333
We do not know her.

1392
01:13:46,917 --> 01:13:49,542
We do not know, right, how she…

1393
01:13:51,542 --> 01:13:54,167
What is truth? Right?
With various sources.

1394
01:13:54,250 --> 01:13:56,708
We don't know that… We don't…
(hesitates) What exists?

1395
01:13:56,792 --> 01:13:58,417
Does any of this exist?

1396
01:13:58,500 --> 01:14:01,125
So…

1397
01:14:01,208 --> 01:14:02,500
Well said, Doc.

1398
01:14:02,583 --> 01:14:03,750
Thank you.

1399
01:14:04,458 --> 01:14:07,083
(Simone) You promised if I stuck with you,
you could heal me.

1400
01:14:08,292 --> 01:14:09,500
If that's true,

1401
01:14:10,042 --> 01:14:11,667
I don't need you to be a saint.

1402
01:14:12,167 --> 01:14:13,708
(Lee) We're with you, Monsignor Wicks.

1403
01:14:14,375 --> 01:14:18,833
And literally nothing that you say or do
is gonna change that.

1404
01:14:24,417 --> 01:14:25,833
(inhales deeply)

1405
01:14:25,917 --> 01:14:28,667
I will give my final service

1406
01:14:30,083 --> 01:14:32,500
a week from today on Easter Sunday.

1407
01:14:33,792 --> 01:14:35,208
And then

1408
01:14:35,958 --> 01:14:39,875
I will close the doors
of this sad little church for good.

1409
01:14:39,958 --> 01:14:42,542
(Wicks breathes deeply)

1410
01:14:43,250 --> 01:14:47,500
But not before I have destroyed
each and every one of you.

1411
01:14:48,083 --> 01:14:50,667
(tense music plays)

1412
01:14:50,750 --> 01:14:51,958
Sorry. Wait, what?

1413
01:14:52,042 --> 01:14:53,458
Your drinking, Nat?

1414
01:14:53,542 --> 01:14:54,750
Yeah. What?

1415
01:14:54,833 --> 01:14:56,583
Oh, you're a dangerous man.

1416
01:14:57,333 --> 01:14:58,750
Going to work drunk.

1417
01:14:58,833 --> 01:15:01,917
Treating patients, children, while drunk.

1418
01:15:02,708 --> 01:15:04,542
This community should know.

1419
01:15:04,625 --> 01:15:06,708
The medical board should know.

1420
01:15:06,792 --> 01:15:11,167
No one must ever trust or hire you again.

1421
01:15:11,792 --> 01:15:12,875
And, Lee.

1422
01:15:13,500 --> 01:15:16,500
This, uh, Troubadour book
you've been writing.

1423
01:15:16,583 --> 01:15:21,292
Its boot licking idiocy
is an affront to my ministry.

1424
01:15:21,375 --> 01:15:25,208
It… It's my duty to warn
not only the public but… (inhales)

1425
01:15:25,292 --> 01:15:27,292
…my friends in the publishing world.

1426
01:15:27,375 --> 01:15:30,250
It must be buried. You must be buried.

1427
01:15:30,833 --> 01:15:34,458
Exposed as the irrelevant clown
that you are.

1428
01:15:34,542 --> 01:15:36,958
What the hell?
What is even happening right now?

1429
01:15:37,042 --> 01:15:38,125
(Wicks) And, Vera.

1430
01:15:38,667 --> 01:15:41,000
You are your father's nightmare.

1431
01:15:41,792 --> 01:15:43,417
He would be so ashamed.

1432
01:15:45,333 --> 01:15:48,417
Simone. I cannot heal a faithless woman.

1433
01:15:49,125 --> 01:15:50,542
I cannot help you.

1434
01:15:50,625 --> 01:15:53,125
You said you could cast it out of me.

1435
01:15:53,208 --> 01:15:55,000
Mm, I promised you nothing.

1436
01:15:56,167 --> 01:15:58,792
I've given you all of my savings.

1437
01:15:58,875 --> 01:16:00,958
You cannot buy God's healing.

1438
01:16:01,750 --> 01:16:03,583
You will never be healed.

1439
01:16:03,667 --> 01:16:06,500
You will die in pain
in the prison of that chair.

1440
01:16:07,125 --> 01:16:10,167
Why are you doing this?
I don't understand.

1441
01:16:10,250 --> 01:16:13,417
- (Lee) This is a joke. Right? A joke.
- (Nat) I am so confused.

1442
01:16:13,500 --> 01:16:16,750
Is this payback for the Father Jud prayer
meeting because he ambushed us.

1443
01:16:16,833 --> 01:16:18,417
Father Jud's prayer meeting?

1444
01:16:19,875 --> 01:16:21,792
I have kept this church.

1445
01:16:21,875 --> 01:16:24,000
I have fortified it with the truth of God.

1446
01:16:24,083 --> 01:16:27,917
And now the betrayal to find my authority

1447
01:16:28,000 --> 01:16:31,292
- and faith and life itself challenged…
- (door opens)

1448
01:16:31,375 --> 01:16:33,792
…and from inside my own sanctuary!

1449
01:16:36,333 --> 01:16:37,542
Get out!

1450
01:16:39,500 --> 01:16:41,750
- (door slams)
- Weak.

1451
01:16:42,583 --> 01:16:44,000
All of you.

1452
01:16:44,083 --> 01:16:46,292
You can't follow my path.

1453
01:16:46,375 --> 01:16:48,583
Yes, we are at war

1454
01:16:48,667 --> 01:16:51,125
and I cast you out of my fortress.

1455
01:16:51,708 --> 01:16:52,917
You son of a bitch.

1456
01:16:53,000 --> 01:16:55,875
On Easter Sunday,
when the pews fill with townspeople,

1457
01:16:55,958 --> 01:16:58,375
I will lay bare the sins of this flock.

1458
01:16:58,458 --> 01:17:02,875
Cut you loose and shake the dust
of this place off of my sandals.

1459
01:17:04,083 --> 01:17:05,292
And to hell

1460
01:17:06,625 --> 01:17:07,708
with you all.

1461
01:17:07,792 --> 01:17:09,792
(sinister music rises)

1462
01:17:16,958 --> 01:17:18,167
(music stops)

1463
01:17:21,417 --> 01:17:25,583
(inhales sharply) Well, glory be.
That cleared the room. (Scoffs)

1464
01:17:25,667 --> 01:17:26,750
Cy.

1465
01:17:28,042 --> 01:17:30,125
- Why'd he do that?
- (sighs)

1466
01:17:30,208 --> 01:17:32,458
(Jud) Cy. Tell me. What was happening?

1467
01:17:32,542 --> 01:17:34,917
Why'd he torch them all?
Why would he do that?

1468
01:17:35,000 --> 01:17:36,333
Because I told him to.

1469
01:17:37,292 --> 01:17:39,917
When Vera told me the truth,
I went and found him.

1470
01:17:40,792 --> 01:17:44,000
<i>And he embraced me as a son
for the first time in my life.</i>

1471
01:17:44,750 --> 01:17:46,667
He unburdened himself.

1472
01:17:47,375 --> 01:17:49,375
(Wicks) I hate this place.

1473
01:17:50,542 --> 01:17:52,958
I hate this sad flock of losers.

1474
01:17:53,792 --> 01:17:55,417
I want to get out.

1475
01:17:56,208 --> 01:17:57,833
And now, finally…

1476
01:17:58,958 --> 01:18:00,167
I can.

1477
01:18:01,958 --> 01:18:03,167
He told me,

1478
01:18:03,958 --> 01:18:06,792
his grandfather's family fortune,
lost all these years,

1479
01:18:06,875 --> 01:18:09,083
he told me he found it. Just this week.

1480
01:18:09,167 --> 01:18:11,000
No. No, that money is gone.

1481
01:18:11,083 --> 01:18:14,792
Nobody knows where Prentice put it,
but it's gone without a trace.

1482
01:18:14,875 --> 01:18:17,500
- He told me he found it.
- (chuckles derisively)

1483
01:18:17,583 --> 01:18:20,625
(Cy) He was gonna shutter this dump
and retire in filthy wealth.

1484
01:18:21,292 --> 01:18:24,417
And I told him, "Are you nuts?"

1485
01:18:24,500 --> 01:18:27,292
Retire? Do you know the power
of what you do on that stage?

1486
01:18:27,375 --> 01:18:28,625
I've shrunk the flock.

1487
01:18:28,708 --> 01:18:30,375
(Cy) No. You've radicalized them.

1488
01:18:31,042 --> 01:18:32,083
That is power.

1489
01:18:32,875 --> 01:18:36,875
In a small town, there are only so many
witches to burn and zealots to activate.

1490
01:18:36,958 --> 01:18:39,375
Your flame lacks fuel.

1491
01:18:39,458 --> 01:18:40,875
But on the Internet,

1492
01:18:41,375 --> 01:18:42,583
wildfire.

1493
01:18:43,875 --> 01:18:45,083
This money.

1494
01:18:45,875 --> 01:18:48,708
Your cult of personality.
Are you kidding me?

1495
01:18:48,792 --> 01:18:50,333
Give me four years.

1496
01:18:50,417 --> 01:18:51,833
You could be president.

1497
01:18:52,917 --> 01:18:55,042
Together we can build a real empire.

1498
01:18:56,250 --> 01:18:59,250
As father and son.

1499
01:19:01,667 --> 01:19:03,083
Like in <i>Star Wars?</i>

1500
01:19:03,167 --> 01:19:05,958
- Yeah. Exactly, like the Rebels.
- Oh.

1501
01:19:06,042 --> 01:19:09,458
His ministry and my political instincts
fueled by enough money.

1502
01:19:09,542 --> 01:19:11,833
Can you imagine
what we could do in Christ's name?

1503
01:19:12,500 --> 01:19:14,125
Yeah. Yeah, I think I can.

1504
01:19:14,208 --> 01:19:17,542
First, I told him,
and I'll admit this is a little personal,

1505
01:19:17,625 --> 01:19:20,375
first I told him
we need to burn this flock.

1506
01:19:20,458 --> 01:19:21,833
They're a liability.

1507
01:19:21,917 --> 01:19:24,042
If they associate themselves with us,

1508
01:19:24,125 --> 01:19:27,000
show up on cable news,
even want a place in this thing…

1509
01:19:27,083 --> 01:19:29,333
We need to burn them off like leeches.

1510
01:19:30,250 --> 01:19:31,875
(Jud) <i>That's why he torched them all.</i>

1511
01:19:32,542 --> 01:19:34,375
'Cause of your petty vindictiveness.

1512
01:19:34,958 --> 01:19:37,500
One of them might have killed him for it.
You know that, right?

1513
01:19:38,083 --> 01:19:40,917
Getting back to this vast fortune.

1514
01:19:41,500 --> 01:19:42,792
So it's yours now?

1515
01:19:42,875 --> 01:19:44,625
- Technically, yes.
- Technically?

1516
01:19:45,208 --> 01:19:47,417
- He didn't tell you where it was.
- (Cy) No.

1517
01:19:48,000 --> 01:19:50,208
His accounts are empty. There's nothing.

1518
01:19:51,083 --> 01:19:52,083
So where is it?

1519
01:19:52,708 --> 01:19:55,292
And then, I realized, 50 years ago,

1520
01:19:55,375 --> 01:19:59,125
what was the safest way
for Prentice to hide $80 million?

1521
01:19:59,708 --> 01:20:02,500
- A Swiss bank account.
- (Benoit) Aha!

1522
01:20:03,000 --> 01:20:06,417
And so all you need to do
is find that account number.

1523
01:20:07,333 --> 01:20:08,750
No luck there?

1524
01:20:08,833 --> 01:20:11,583
(sighs in exasperation) It has to be
written down somewhere.

1525
01:20:11,667 --> 01:20:13,917
Martha files everything and it isn't here.

1526
01:20:14,000 --> 01:20:15,208
I don't know.

1527
01:20:15,792 --> 01:20:18,667
Here. I thought it might be a code
because he kept saying,

1528
01:20:18,750 --> 01:20:20,542
"Eve's Apple
would be restored to the tree."

1529
01:20:20,625 --> 01:20:24,208
That was a thing.
As if Eve's Apple is the fortune.

1530
01:20:24,292 --> 01:20:26,750
But a Swiss account,
we're looking for 19 numbers,

1531
01:20:26,833 --> 01:20:28,042
so it doesn't work.

1532
01:20:28,583 --> 01:20:30,708
Vera, did he ever tell you anything?

1533
01:20:31,583 --> 01:20:34,708
Even if he did, I would go to my grave
before giving it to you.

1534
01:20:35,500 --> 01:20:36,583
Yeah.

1535
01:20:37,667 --> 01:20:40,917
You'd have done anything to keep
the prodigal son from getting the fortune.

1536
01:20:41,000 --> 01:20:42,208
It burns you up.

1537
01:20:42,917 --> 01:20:44,333
You bitter hag.

1538
01:20:45,375 --> 01:20:46,792
That money

1539
01:20:47,375 --> 01:20:52,792
is one psalm in the Bible
of my bitterness, you fucking child.

1540
01:20:53,458 --> 01:20:57,542
You should come and get your shit,
it'll be out on the street. (Scoffs)

1541
01:21:01,000 --> 01:21:03,125
(door opens, closes)

1542
01:21:03,208 --> 01:21:06,625
You. You're a detective. I'll pay you.
I don't care, this is very important,

1543
01:21:06,708 --> 01:21:09,542
my inheritance
and future political career depends on it.

1544
01:21:09,625 --> 01:21:11,750
Can you think of anything

1545
01:21:11,833 --> 01:21:15,250
related to Eve's Apple
that might contain that number?

1546
01:21:17,208 --> 01:21:20,292
Oh, um… Mm-mm. (Sniffles)

1547
01:21:20,917 --> 01:21:22,750
But if you think of anything,
you'll call me?

1548
01:21:22,833 --> 01:21:24,833
- Oh, yeah. You bet.
- All right.

1549
01:21:25,625 --> 01:21:26,792
(engine starts)

1550
01:21:26,875 --> 01:21:28,917
(intriguing music plays)

1551
01:21:32,208 --> 01:21:33,542
We should look everywhere.

1552
01:21:38,458 --> 01:21:41,542
It might be, uh, sewn in the lining.

1553
01:21:42,167 --> 01:21:44,458
- Etched in the metal.
- (ripping)

1554
01:21:53,958 --> 01:21:55,083
(Benoit sighs)

1555
01:22:00,167 --> 01:22:01,167
(hollow thudding)

1556
01:22:04,875 --> 01:22:06,167
This is hollow.

1557
01:22:06,750 --> 01:22:08,167
Yeah. Do it.

1558
01:22:16,083 --> 01:22:17,292
(sighs)

1559
01:22:24,125 --> 01:22:25,125
(sighs)

1560
01:22:25,792 --> 01:22:26,792
(clatters)

1561
01:22:29,625 --> 01:22:31,250
Remind me to file this.

1562
01:22:31,333 --> 01:22:32,542
File that.

1563
01:22:33,792 --> 01:22:35,750
- It doesn't make sense.
- I know.

1564
01:22:35,833 --> 01:22:37,875
An 80-million-dollar fortune.

1565
01:22:37,958 --> 01:22:39,708
But if Eve's Apple is the fortune

1566
01:22:39,792 --> 01:22:42,875
and it's not a pile of cash
in a Swiss account somewhere, what is it?

1567
01:22:47,000 --> 01:22:47,833
What?

1568
01:22:47,917 --> 01:22:50,000
They must have
misprinted the date on this.

1569
01:22:51,083 --> 01:22:54,583
It says the crypt opening thing
was ordered last Wednesday.

1570
01:22:55,250 --> 01:22:56,667
That can't be right.

1571
01:22:58,542 --> 01:23:01,750
Who would preorder burial equipment
for a man who isn't dead?

1572
01:23:03,125 --> 01:23:06,250
Someone who knew with great certainty
when their day and hour would come.

1573
01:23:06,333 --> 01:23:07,542
Give me that.

1574
01:23:08,583 --> 01:23:11,375
Oh, that's computer printed.
That's not a misprint. That's it.

1575
01:23:11,458 --> 01:23:13,917
Whoever called in that order,
that's the key.

1576
01:23:14,000 --> 01:23:15,583
- Okay. Yeah. Yeah.
- (line ringing)

1577
01:23:15,667 --> 01:23:18,083
- (telephone ringing)
- (pop music playing faintly)

1578
01:23:19,333 --> 01:23:21,458
Steel Wheels Construction. This is Louise.

1579
01:23:21,542 --> 01:23:24,083
Hello, Louise. It's Father Jud
from Perpetual Fortitude.

1580
01:23:25,250 --> 01:23:27,417
- Oh. Hello.
<i>- Hi, Louise.</i>

1581
01:23:27,500 --> 01:23:29,917
We had a piece
of your construction equipment here today.

1582
01:23:30,000 --> 01:23:32,583
- Uh, a forklift to open a, um… a crypt.
<i>- Oh, yeah. I know.</i>

1583
01:23:32,667 --> 01:23:35,042
<i>It's not too often
we get a crypt opening order.</i>

1584
01:23:35,125 --> 01:23:36,458
Great. So I need to know...

1585
01:23:36,542 --> 01:23:38,875
<i>I actually processed that order.
I do all the processing.</i>

1586
01:23:38,958 --> 01:23:40,625
Yeah. What I need to know, Louise, is...

1587
01:23:40,708 --> 01:23:42,708
<i>- I run this place with my brother James.</i>
- Right.

1588
01:23:42,792 --> 01:23:44,917
<i>- He takes orders but I process them.</i>
- Yeah. Right.

1589
01:23:45,000 --> 01:23:47,000
So the reason I'm calling, Louise, is to...

1590
01:23:47,083 --> 01:23:49,833
<i>I've been to that church of yours,
but I don't think you were there.</i>

1591
01:23:49,917 --> 01:23:52,917
- No, I… I'm new, relatively new here.
<i>- Congratulations.</i>

1592
01:23:53,000 --> 01:23:55,750
- Louise, I… I have to ask…
<i>- No, it was an older guy.</i>

1593
01:23:55,833 --> 01:23:58,208
<i>- Father… Is he…</i>
- Monsignor, Monsignor.

1594
01:23:58,292 --> 01:24:00,042
<i>- Father Monsignor, okay, well…</i>
- Louise...

1595
01:24:00,125 --> 01:24:03,625
<i>He was preaching when I went and
I gotta tell you, that is not a nice man.</i>

1596
01:24:03,708 --> 01:24:06,500
<i>- But I am sorry that he…</i>
- Okay.

1597
01:24:06,583 --> 01:24:09,000
<i>…yikes, died and,
you know, for all y'all's loss…</i>

1598
01:24:09,083 --> 01:24:11,500
Yeah, it's a terrible tragedy
for everyone, Louise.

1599
01:24:11,583 --> 01:24:14,000
Can I… I have to, uh, interrupt.

1600
01:24:14,083 --> 01:24:16,083
- I have a question.
<i>- Yeah.</i>

1601
01:24:16,167 --> 01:24:19,542
Uh, the order for the forklift.
I need to know who placed the order.

1602
01:24:19,625 --> 01:24:22,042
<i>- James takes the orders and…</i>
- James takes the orders.

1603
01:24:22,125 --> 01:24:24,708
<i>- …he's left for the day.</i>
- Can I have James' number?

1604
01:24:24,792 --> 01:24:27,417
This is very important. We need to
find out who placed that order.

1605
01:24:27,500 --> 01:24:30,875
<i>- No, no. I don't think I can do that…</i>
- No, it's very important.

1606
01:24:30,958 --> 01:24:33,083
<i>- Excuse me, Father.</i>
- It's very...

1607
01:24:33,167 --> 01:24:35,167
<i>What I can do, as I was saying,</i>

1608
01:24:35,250 --> 01:24:38,125
<i>is I can get that information for you
and then I will give you</i>

1609
01:24:38,208 --> 01:24:39,833
<i>- a buzz back.</i>
- That's it. That's great.

1610
01:24:39,917 --> 01:24:42,542
And if you could call James now,
I would appreciate it so much.

1611
01:24:42,625 --> 01:24:44,542
- Thank you, Louise.
- And she'll call you back.

1612
01:24:44,625 --> 01:24:46,708
<i>I will. Hey, Father,
could I ask you something?</i>

1613
01:24:46,792 --> 01:24:49,000
Yeah, it's… Though, I mean…

1614
01:24:49,583 --> 01:24:51,083
Well, if you can make it quick.

1615
01:24:51,167 --> 01:24:54,125
- This is a priority for us right now.
- Maybe she could call you back and...

1616
01:24:54,208 --> 01:24:56,208
<i>Father Jud would you… Could you…</i>

1617
01:24:57,708 --> 01:24:58,792
Louise?

1618
01:24:58,875 --> 01:25:00,583
- (scoffs)
- (Louise) <i>Oh, God.</i>

1619
01:25:02,250 --> 01:25:03,333
Louise?

1620
01:25:03,958 --> 01:25:05,958
(sighs) <i>Will you pray for me?</i>

1621
01:25:09,500 --> 01:25:10,500
Uh…

1622
01:25:11,375 --> 01:25:13,000
Yeah, of course.

1623
01:25:14,417 --> 01:25:17,250
- Can I ask what for?
- (Louise sniffles) <i>Uh…</i>

1624
01:25:18,708 --> 01:25:20,333
<i>It's, uh, my mother.</i>

1625
01:25:22,667 --> 01:25:23,875
She's sick?

1626
01:25:24,625 --> 01:25:25,708
<i>Yeah.</i>

1627
01:25:25,792 --> 01:25:28,333
<i>Um, she's in hospice.</i>

1628
01:25:29,708 --> 01:25:31,333
I'm so sorry, Louise.

1629
01:25:31,417 --> 01:25:33,417
<i>Uh, she won't talk to me.</i>

1630
01:25:33,500 --> 01:25:35,583
<i>We fought last time we talked.</i>

1631
01:25:35,667 --> 01:25:41,458
<i>Uh, she has a tumor in her brain
that's affecting her,</i>

1632
01:25:41,542 --> 01:25:45,083
<i>and it's making her say
really terrible things,</i>

1633
01:25:45,167 --> 01:25:47,292
<i>and so I said bad things back</i>

1634
01:25:47,375 --> 01:25:50,083
<i>and now I'm afraid that
that's gonna be the last thing</i>

1635
01:25:50,167 --> 01:25:52,167
<i>that we ever say to each other.</i>

1636
01:25:54,833 --> 01:25:56,917
(tearfully) Father, I, um…

1637
01:25:58,833 --> 01:26:02,250
I'm feeling pretty alone, um, right now.

1638
01:26:05,542 --> 01:26:08,750
- (crying softly)
- I'm so sorry, Louise.

1639
01:26:10,083 --> 01:26:11,292
You're not alone.

1640
01:26:12,750 --> 01:26:14,167
I'm right here.

1641
01:26:14,958 --> 01:26:16,167
I'm here.

1642
01:26:17,042 --> 01:26:18,542
Can you tell me your mother's name?

1643
01:26:23,625 --> 01:26:24,917
(clicks tongue softly)

1644
01:26:26,167 --> 01:26:27,333
(sighs softly)

1645
01:26:27,417 --> 01:26:30,417
- (thunder rumbling)
- (wind gusting)

1646
01:26:32,875 --> 01:26:33,875
(inhales)

1647
01:26:34,875 --> 01:26:36,208
(exhales sharply)

1648
01:26:47,458 --> 01:26:50,083
I pray that Barbara
may feel her daughter's love.

1649
01:26:51,167 --> 01:26:55,000
That it will comfort her in this time,
and, Lord, I pray for Louise.

1650
01:26:56,417 --> 01:26:58,625
Be with her
and give her wisdom and guidance.

1651
01:26:58,708 --> 01:27:02,125
Hold her in your healing arms
and let her know she is loved.

1652
01:27:02,667 --> 01:27:04,292
She is not alone.

1653
01:27:04,917 --> 01:27:08,333
This we pray
through Christ our Lord. Amen.

1654
01:27:09,167 --> 01:27:10,167
Okay, Louise.

1655
01:27:10,750 --> 01:27:13,417
You have my number.
Any time, day or night,

1656
01:27:13,500 --> 01:27:14,792
I'm here for you.

1657
01:27:15,292 --> 01:27:17,250
- This church is here for you.
- (door opens)

1658
01:27:17,333 --> 01:27:18,500
Bless you. Okay.

1659
01:27:19,042 --> 01:27:22,042
(panting) Storm. I came to close up.

1660
01:27:23,792 --> 01:27:26,417
(Jud) I'll get the church.
You take care of the rectory.

1661
01:27:30,375 --> 01:27:32,625
- (wind gusting)
- Don't follow me, Blanc. I'm done.

1662
01:27:32,708 --> 01:27:34,542
And, uh, why exactly?

1663
01:27:34,625 --> 01:27:37,083
I've had a "road to Damascus" thing.

1664
01:27:37,167 --> 01:27:39,750
Paul had a holy revelation
on the road to Damascus.

1665
01:27:39,833 --> 01:27:42,708
Yes, I know. He was struck blind
and all that hogwash.

1666
01:27:42,792 --> 01:27:44,792
Probably just a case of pink eye.

1667
01:27:44,875 --> 01:27:48,375
But he was not on the verge
of solving a murder when it happened.

1668
01:27:48,458 --> 01:27:50,875
I mean, what do you think
we're doing here?

1669
01:27:51,542 --> 01:27:54,958
Why do you think I became a priest?
No bullshit. Really. Why?

1670
01:27:55,042 --> 01:27:58,125
- (wind howling)
- (thunder rumbling)

1671
01:27:58,208 --> 01:27:59,417
You felt guilt.

1672
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:02,000
For taking a life. And the church,

1673
01:28:02,083 --> 01:28:04,917
it offered you a place to hide
and a clear method

1674
01:28:05,000 --> 01:28:07,000
to give you a sense of absolution.

1675
01:28:07,625 --> 01:28:10,500
The guy I killed in the ring, I hated him.

1676
01:28:11,000 --> 01:28:12,833
I remember, I knew he was in trouble

1677
01:28:12,917 --> 01:28:15,125
and I kept going and going
until I felt him break.

1678
01:28:15,208 --> 01:28:17,833
It wasn't an accident.
I killed him with hate in my heart.

1679
01:28:17,917 --> 01:28:20,250
There's no hiding from that,
there's no solving it.

1680
01:28:20,333 --> 01:28:24,167
God didn't hide me or fix me.
He loves me when I'm guilty.

1681
01:28:24,250 --> 01:28:26,375
That's what I should be doing
for these people.

1682
01:28:26,458 --> 01:28:27,750
Not this whodunnit game.

1683
01:28:27,833 --> 01:28:29,083
No, now wait a minute.

1684
01:28:29,167 --> 01:28:30,542
(wind gusting)

1685
01:28:35,375 --> 01:28:37,583
Excuse me. Excuse me, I...

1686
01:28:38,333 --> 01:28:40,167
Would you look at me
when I'm talking to you?

1687
01:28:40,250 --> 01:28:42,250
We're looking for a murderer.
This is not a game.

1688
01:28:42,333 --> 01:28:43,708
It is a game!

1689
01:28:43,792 --> 01:28:45,417
Solving it, winning it.

1690
01:28:45,500 --> 01:28:47,542
Getting your big checkmate moment.

1691
01:28:47,625 --> 01:28:51,458
And by using me in it, you're setting me
against my real and only purpose in life.

1692
01:28:51,542 --> 01:28:54,167
Which is not to fight the wicked
and bring them to justice,

1693
01:28:54,250 --> 01:28:57,458
but to serve them
and bring them to Christ.

1694
01:28:57,542 --> 01:28:59,375
Otherwise, I'm just as bad as Wicks.

1695
01:28:59,458 --> 01:29:01,458
Making it about me and not Jesus.

1696
01:29:02,500 --> 01:29:04,917
Listen, you don't
have to understand, Blanc.

1697
01:29:05,000 --> 01:29:06,542
But just please,

1698
01:29:06,625 --> 01:29:08,917
please, please, please let me be.

1699
01:29:09,000 --> 01:29:12,625
- (intriguing music plays)
- (thunder rumbling)

1700
01:29:15,625 --> 01:29:17,458
- Can you say that again?
- No.

1701
01:29:17,542 --> 01:29:20,417
About making it about you, not Jesus.
Like Wicks, you said.

1702
01:29:20,500 --> 01:29:22,708
Father, this is important.

1703
01:29:22,792 --> 01:29:24,292
Help me understand!

1704
01:29:24,375 --> 01:29:27,375
We are here to serve the world,
not beat it.

1705
01:29:28,125 --> 01:29:30,333
- That's what Christ did.
- So?

1706
01:29:30,417 --> 01:29:33,250
So when Wicks was talking about
fighting the world for Christ's sake,

1707
01:29:33,333 --> 01:29:36,792
he wasn't talking about Christ,
he was talking about his own ego.

1708
01:29:36,875 --> 01:29:39,708
And power.
He was never talking about Christ.

1709
01:29:41,833 --> 01:29:45,042
Yes, over and over
he talked about Christ rising in power.

1710
01:29:45,125 --> 01:29:47,042
Getting his revenge on the unfaithful.

1711
01:29:47,125 --> 01:29:48,958
Eve's Apple is the treasure.

1712
01:29:49,042 --> 01:29:51,458
"Eve's Apple restored to the tree."

1713
01:29:51,542 --> 01:29:52,875
Now, what does that mean?

1714
01:29:52,958 --> 01:29:55,375
Blanc. I don't know.

1715
01:29:56,292 --> 01:29:57,917
And I don't care.

1716
01:29:58,542 --> 01:30:01,292
(sirens approaching)

1717
01:30:01,375 --> 01:30:02,875
(thunder rumbling)

1718
01:30:03,875 --> 01:30:06,625
That'll be Geraldine
coming for her update on the case.

1719
01:30:06,708 --> 01:30:09,333
Now, Father, you're right.

1720
01:30:09,417 --> 01:30:11,417
This is my game, not yours.

1721
01:30:11,500 --> 01:30:14,708
Why don't you head back to the rectory?
I'll handle her.

1722
01:30:16,292 --> 01:30:17,500
Thank you.

1723
01:30:18,208 --> 01:30:20,333
Make sure the door's shut when you leave.

1724
01:30:23,750 --> 01:30:25,583
Hope you catch your killer, Blanc.

1725
01:30:26,458 --> 01:30:27,833
Thank you. I… I will.

1726
01:30:27,917 --> 01:30:29,333
(sirens wailing)

1727
01:30:35,958 --> 01:30:37,958
(indistinct police radio chatter)

1728
01:30:45,250 --> 01:30:46,667
Father Jud?

1729
01:30:47,333 --> 01:30:49,083
- Father Jud.
- He's not here.

1730
01:30:49,167 --> 01:30:50,167
Come.

1731
01:30:50,667 --> 01:30:53,875
I want you to search those back rooms
and that closet thing too.

1732
01:30:53,958 --> 01:30:55,833
(thunder rumbling distantly)

1733
01:30:57,250 --> 01:30:58,250
Oh.

1734
01:30:59,167 --> 01:31:00,583
It's good, right?

1735
01:31:00,667 --> 01:31:01,958
(Geraldine) Great, actually.

1736
01:31:02,042 --> 01:31:04,375
Especially the part where
Gideon Fell walks you through

1737
01:31:04,458 --> 01:31:06,375
the possible solutions
of a locked-door crime.

1738
01:31:06,458 --> 01:31:07,458
- Mm.
- Yeah.

1739
01:31:07,500 --> 01:31:09,667
You covered three of them,
then you stopped.

1740
01:31:10,292 --> 01:31:12,500
Now, having read the fourth, I know why.

1741
01:31:13,125 --> 01:31:15,208
See, I rewatched the video
and I realized something.

1742
01:31:15,292 --> 01:31:16,333
(suspenseful music plays)

1743
01:31:16,417 --> 01:31:18,625
<i>From the moment Jud enters the closet,</i>

1744
01:31:19,125 --> 01:31:23,292
<i>until the first of the flock
has a line of sight into that closet</i>

1745
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:25,417
is nine seconds.

1746
01:31:25,917 --> 01:31:28,750
Nine seconds alone and unseen.

1747
01:31:29,667 --> 01:31:33,500
<i>Plenty of time to do the deed
with a concealed knife.</i>

1748
01:31:37,167 --> 01:31:39,000
That's how it was done, right?

1749
01:31:39,083 --> 01:31:40,292
No games.

1750
01:31:40,792 --> 01:31:43,417
No bullshit. That's how it was done.

1751
01:31:43,500 --> 01:31:45,292
(thunder rumbling distantly)

1752
01:31:45,375 --> 01:31:47,042
- Yes.
- (scoffs)

1753
01:31:48,250 --> 01:31:50,875
And you knew. You knew all along
and you toyed with that poor kid

1754
01:31:50,958 --> 01:31:52,583
- like a cat with a mouse.
- No.

1755
01:31:52,667 --> 01:31:55,167
I don't have the whole picture just yet.

1756
01:31:55,250 --> 01:31:57,500
- If you could give me a little more time…
- No.

1757
01:31:57,583 --> 01:31:59,875
- I'm gonna be able to get...
- No!

1758
01:31:59,958 --> 01:32:02,375
I found my killer and I'm bringing him in.

1759
01:32:03,208 --> 01:32:04,417
Where is he?

1760
01:32:04,958 --> 01:32:07,917
- (thunder crashing)
- (wind gusting)

1761
01:32:12,750 --> 01:32:14,958
(slow suspenseful music plays)

1762
01:32:24,417 --> 01:32:26,500
(breathing heavily)

1763
01:32:27,875 --> 01:32:29,667
(muffled thudding)

1764
01:32:38,167 --> 01:32:40,333
(thudding continues)

1765
01:32:52,625 --> 01:32:55,333
(muffled thudding)

1766
01:33:02,625 --> 01:33:03,958
(deep rumbling)

1767
01:33:15,333 --> 01:33:16,875
(breathing heavily)

1768
01:33:40,583 --> 01:33:41,583
(Jud) Sam!

1769
01:33:42,000 --> 01:33:43,958
(panting)

1770
01:33:48,292 --> 01:33:49,542
(yelps, groans)

1771
01:33:53,625 --> 01:33:56,333
(panting)

1772
01:34:00,042 --> 01:34:03,042
- (ominous music plays)
- (high-pitched distortion)

1773
01:34:08,583 --> 01:34:10,583
(panting echoing)

1774
01:34:20,667 --> 01:34:22,333
(breathing heavily)

1775
01:34:26,125 --> 01:34:28,167
(rhythmic thumping)

1776
01:34:31,250 --> 01:34:33,083
(thumping accelerates)

1777
01:34:36,625 --> 01:34:38,667
(distorted yelling)

1778
01:34:49,542 --> 01:34:51,958
- (suspenseful music plays)
- (gasps)

1779
01:34:53,542 --> 01:34:56,250
(gasps, groans)

1780
01:34:56,333 --> 01:34:58,208
(panting)

1781
01:34:58,292 --> 01:34:59,500
(Benoit) Who's there?

1782
01:35:02,708 --> 01:35:04,250
(gasps, grunts)

1783
01:35:04,833 --> 01:35:06,042
Wait!

1784
01:35:13,625 --> 01:35:14,708
(Geraldine) Blanc?

1785
01:35:14,792 --> 01:35:15,875
Here.

1786
01:35:16,542 --> 01:35:19,458
(gasps) Oh, shit. Who's that?

1787
01:35:19,542 --> 01:35:21,375
The groundskeeper, Samson.

1788
01:35:22,875 --> 01:35:24,708
What the hell happened?

1789
01:35:39,125 --> 01:35:40,250
Oh…

1790
01:35:41,208 --> 01:35:43,708
(Benoit) Mm. (Mutters, clears throat)

1791
01:35:44,958 --> 01:35:45,958
(Geraldine) Uh…

1792
01:35:49,625 --> 01:35:51,583
Mm. (Clicks tongue) Yeah.

1793
01:35:51,667 --> 01:35:52,667
Okay.

1794
01:35:53,208 --> 01:35:56,625
Okay, Wicks was 100% medically dead dead.

1795
01:35:56,708 --> 01:35:59,125
I mean, we know this, I'm just…

1796
01:35:59,625 --> 01:36:01,042
Just saying, right?

1797
01:36:02,333 --> 01:36:03,417
Right.

1798
01:36:05,667 --> 01:36:08,875
(Geraldine) Okay,
then I can also say out loud,

1799
01:36:09,458 --> 01:36:11,875
a man can't just rise from the dead.

1800
01:36:11,958 --> 01:36:14,792
I mean, there's obviously some
<i>Scooby-Doo </i>shit going on here.

1801
01:36:15,292 --> 01:36:16,708
"Scooby-Dooby-Doo."

1802
01:36:16,792 --> 01:36:20,625
Praise to God!
Praise and glory to the Almighty!

1803
01:36:20,708 --> 01:36:22,125
- Praise Him!
- (siren wails)

1804
01:36:22,208 --> 01:36:26,125
Praise God!
Praise and glory to the Almighty.

1805
01:36:26,208 --> 01:36:29,000
- He hath raised His Son.
- Hey, Ritz.

1806
01:36:29,083 --> 01:36:30,500
Set a perimeter on the road.

1807
01:36:30,583 --> 01:36:33,000
News is gonna spread fast
and I don't want any lookie-loos.

1808
01:36:33,083 --> 01:36:34,500
- You got it.
- Chief!

1809
01:36:34,583 --> 01:36:35,417
What?

1810
01:36:35,500 --> 01:36:37,625
That motion-detector light there,
it's also a camera.

1811
01:36:37,708 --> 01:36:39,958
But it's not hooked up to anything.

1812
01:36:40,042 --> 01:36:41,167
(Geraldine) A camera, huh?

1813
01:36:41,250 --> 01:36:43,750
I don't know. Maybe it's recording
something on a chip inside.

1814
01:36:43,833 --> 01:36:45,958
Why don't you bring it into the media lab?

1815
01:36:46,625 --> 01:36:48,208
Hallelujah, praise God.

1816
01:36:48,292 --> 01:36:50,708
He has raised up
His servant from the dead.

1817
01:36:50,792 --> 01:36:53,417
Hey, do me a favor? Tape off
this entire area, down to the grove.

1818
01:36:53,500 --> 01:36:54,917
- Got it.
- It's a homicide scene.

1819
01:36:55,000 --> 01:36:56,792
The groundskeeper is dead.

1820
01:36:56,875 --> 01:36:58,875
(somber music plays)

1821
01:37:04,833 --> 01:37:07,792
(screams, cries)

1822
01:37:08,958 --> 01:37:10,750
(sobbing) No! Please!

1823
01:37:11,792 --> 01:37:14,208
- Oh, shit.
- (Martha) No! No, no, no!

1824
01:37:14,292 --> 01:37:15,708
(Geraldine) Can I get some help?

1825
01:37:15,792 --> 01:37:17,792
- Get help! Martha.
- No! Oh, no, no!

1826
01:37:17,875 --> 01:37:20,083
- Martha, you need to back up.
- Oh, no!

1827
01:37:20,167 --> 01:37:22,542
- Martha…
- (sobbing)

1828
01:37:22,625 --> 01:37:25,667
Flee into the dark, you murderer!

1829
01:37:25,750 --> 01:37:27,625
- (panting)
- (dramatic music plays)

1830
01:37:27,708 --> 01:37:29,333
But he has returned!

1831
01:37:29,833 --> 01:37:33,542
And he brings vengeance! He brings death!

1832
01:37:34,292 --> 01:37:35,333
(grunts)

1833
01:37:35,417 --> 01:37:36,250
(sniffles)

1834
01:37:36,333 --> 01:37:37,750
- (panting)
- (music fades)

1835
01:37:39,708 --> 01:37:41,375
- (cell phone buzzing)
- (gasps)

1836
01:37:41,458 --> 01:37:42,792
(wind howling)

1837
01:37:46,917 --> 01:37:47,917
(cell phone clacks)

1838
01:37:50,750 --> 01:37:52,167
This is Father Jud.

1839
01:37:52,250 --> 01:37:54,667
<i>Oh, Father Jud, it's Louise.
How you doing?</i>

1840
01:37:56,000 --> 01:37:57,292
Uh…

1841
01:37:58,667 --> 01:38:00,292
Yeah… (hesitates) Hi, Louise.

1842
01:38:00,792 --> 01:38:03,208
<i>I… I hope it's not too late,
but you said it was urgent,</i>

1843
01:38:03,292 --> 01:38:04,917
<i>so I just wanted to tell you…</i>

1844
01:38:05,000 --> 01:38:07,625
<i>I spoke to James
and the order for the forklift</i>

1845
01:38:07,708 --> 01:38:10,333
<i>was actually placed by Monsignor Wicks.</i>

1846
01:38:11,208 --> 01:38:15,292
<i>He spoke to James directly about it,
so I do hope that this clears things up.</i>

1847
01:38:15,917 --> 01:38:19,333
<i>Hey, God bless you, Father,
and you have yourself a good night, okay?</i>

1848
01:38:19,417 --> 01:38:22,000
Uh… Yeah.

1849
01:38:22,667 --> 01:38:25,417
Yeah, you too, Louise. (Pants)

1850
01:38:26,917 --> 01:38:27,917
(cell phone beeps)

1851
01:38:33,500 --> 01:38:35,167
- (sinister music plays)
- (yells)

1852
01:38:37,708 --> 01:38:38,917
(thunderclap)

1853
01:38:40,875 --> 01:38:42,333
(pants)

1854
01:38:48,250 --> 01:38:50,833
- (grunts)
- (cell phone ringing)

1855
01:38:50,917 --> 01:38:52,125
Jeez.

1856
01:38:53,917 --> 01:38:55,000
Yes?

1857
01:38:56,125 --> 01:38:57,958
Slow down, Martha. What?

1858
01:39:00,750 --> 01:39:02,667
- What?
- (thuds)

1859
01:39:02,750 --> 01:39:04,583
- (Lee) <i>It's a miracle.</i>
- Bullshit.

1860
01:39:04,667 --> 01:39:07,083
<i>No, it happened.
Martha said the tomb is empty.</i>

1861
01:39:07,167 --> 01:39:09,375
<i>I'm calling everyone. I'm on my way now.</i>

1862
01:39:15,292 --> 01:39:16,500
Did you, uh…

1863
01:39:17,042 --> 01:39:19,042
What are you doing? You don't smoke.

1864
01:39:19,125 --> 01:39:20,333
I did.

1865
01:39:21,167 --> 01:39:23,000
I smoked for 15 years.

1866
01:39:23,083 --> 01:39:25,000
Did Lee call you? Did he tell you?

1867
01:39:25,500 --> 01:39:26,708
Yep.

1868
01:39:27,958 --> 01:39:30,250
Okay. Well, I'm gonna go
witness a miracle.

1869
01:39:30,333 --> 01:39:33,417
- You enjoy your cigarette indoors.
- (door opens)

1870
01:39:35,083 --> 01:39:36,208
(door closes)

1871
01:39:36,292 --> 01:39:38,333
(vibrates)

1872
01:39:40,875 --> 01:39:43,708
- (heavy knocking on door)
- (slow suspenseful music plays)

1873
01:39:43,792 --> 01:39:45,292
(footsteps approaching)

1874
01:39:55,083 --> 01:39:57,083
(heavy knocking on door)

1875
01:40:05,083 --> 01:40:06,292
Praise be.

1876
01:40:07,417 --> 01:40:08,833
It's accomplished.

1877
01:40:08,917 --> 01:40:10,750
(vibrates)

1878
01:40:10,833 --> 01:40:13,875
- (line ringing)
- Come on.

1879
01:40:15,792 --> 01:40:17,500
- Come on, it's…
- (cell phone beeps)

1880
01:40:18,333 --> 01:40:19,542
He's got it.

1881
01:40:23,042 --> 01:40:26,125
All right, so… it's not great quality…

1882
01:40:26,208 --> 01:40:27,625
- It's fine.
- …but, uh…

1883
01:40:38,458 --> 01:40:39,875
What am I looking at here?

1884
01:40:46,833 --> 01:40:47,833
Okay.

1885
01:40:47,917 --> 01:40:51,375
Um, yeah, so, it records
anytime there's motion

1886
01:40:51,458 --> 01:40:54,875
- and this clip is four seconds later.
- (mouse and keyboard clacking)

1887
01:41:07,042 --> 01:41:09,000
- Okay?
- (knock on door)

1888
01:41:09,083 --> 01:41:11,000
Prints from the gardening tool.

1889
01:41:12,292 --> 01:41:15,958
We didn't run the full database check,
just the suspects you questioned.

1890
01:41:16,667 --> 01:41:17,875
It's Father Jud.

1891
01:41:22,750 --> 01:41:23,958
Where is he?

1892
01:41:24,583 --> 01:41:26,417
I sincerely wish I knew.

1893
01:41:31,208 --> 01:41:33,750
(music intensifies, fades)

1894
01:41:33,833 --> 01:41:35,417
(chiming)

1895
01:41:36,375 --> 01:41:38,083
(thunder rumbling)

1896
01:41:38,167 --> 01:41:39,917
(indistinct police radio chatter)

1897
01:41:46,042 --> 01:41:47,875
Blanc. Blanc!

1898
01:41:48,500 --> 01:41:51,125
- I'm gonna do it. I'm gonna… turn myself...
- (shushes)

1899
01:41:51,208 --> 01:41:53,208
- (officer 1) <i>…388.</i>
- (officer 2) 388, en route.

1900
01:41:53,792 --> 01:41:54,792
(officer 1) <i>433.</i>

1901
01:41:55,625 --> 01:41:57,625
- I'm turning myself in.
- No you are not.

1902
01:41:57,708 --> 01:42:02,000
(on radio, loudly)
<i>♪ Skimbleshanks, the railway cat! ♪</i>

1903
01:42:02,083 --> 01:42:03,083
(Benoit clears throat)

1904
01:42:03,167 --> 01:42:05,917
I did it. I killed Samson.
I'm guilty. I have to confess.

1905
01:42:06,000 --> 01:42:07,083
- Let me out.
- Listen.

1906
01:42:07,167 --> 01:42:09,583
You're gonna tell me
exactly what happened, but right now,

1907
01:42:09,667 --> 01:42:11,292
how do I get to Dr. Nat's house?

1908
01:42:11,375 --> 01:42:12,875
- Dr. Nat?
- Yes, quickly.

1909
01:42:13,375 --> 01:42:14,583
I regret my stalling.

1910
01:42:14,667 --> 01:42:17,000
I only hope we're not too late.
Now, just get down!

1911
01:42:17,083 --> 01:42:19,250
(tires screeching)

1912
01:42:20,000 --> 01:42:21,333
(thunder rumbling)

1913
01:42:21,417 --> 01:42:23,542
Hail Mary, full of grace
the Lord is with you.

1914
01:42:23,625 --> 01:42:25,042
Blessed art thou amongst women…

1915
01:42:25,125 --> 01:42:27,292
…sir, that I respect you.
I respect the badge.

1916
01:42:27,375 --> 01:42:30,583
But this is our church and I'm not telling
you that I'm gonna resort to violence,

1917
01:42:30,667 --> 01:42:34,417
but we're gonna stay here all night
if we have to. We are seeing that crypt!

1918
01:42:34,500 --> 01:42:36,500
- Is it real?
- (Lee) They won't let us in.

1919
01:42:36,583 --> 01:42:39,167
(breath trembling) I need to see.

1920
01:42:39,875 --> 01:42:41,792
Please, I need to see.

1921
01:42:41,875 --> 01:42:43,333
(brakes screech)

1922
01:42:44,458 --> 01:42:46,333
(wind chime tinkling softly)

1923
01:42:48,833 --> 01:42:51,833
(slow suspenseful music plays)

1924
01:42:53,333 --> 01:42:54,875
(door creaking)

1925
01:42:59,542 --> 01:43:00,750
Dr. Nat?

1926
01:43:12,500 --> 01:43:14,083
(glass crunching underfoot)

1927
01:43:30,000 --> 01:43:31,167
(sighs heavily)

1928
01:43:35,625 --> 01:43:37,833
(sniffs, gags) Oh, God.

1929
01:43:38,583 --> 01:43:40,000
What's that smell?

1930
01:43:40,083 --> 01:43:41,792
(Jud breathing heavily)

1931
01:43:45,375 --> 01:43:47,000
Just wait here.

1932
01:43:49,042 --> 01:43:50,125
Blanc.

1933
01:43:50,667 --> 01:43:51,750
(Benoit) Yep.

1934
01:43:53,583 --> 01:43:54,583
(switch clicks)

1935
01:43:55,167 --> 01:43:56,625
(grim music plays)

1936
01:43:56,708 --> 01:43:58,125
Oh, God.

1937
01:44:11,333 --> 01:44:12,417
Right.

1938
01:44:14,083 --> 01:44:18,750
(inhales sharply)
Oh, Lord, that is… (coughs)

1939
01:44:20,958 --> 01:44:23,292
(groaning)

1940
01:44:30,167 --> 01:44:31,250
(Jud) Wicks.

1941
01:44:31,333 --> 01:44:33,500
(Benoit) Yeah, that's… It's him.

1942
01:44:34,375 --> 01:44:35,792
- (Jud) Is he…
- Yeah.

1943
01:44:36,500 --> 01:44:39,958
I mean, for what it's worth
these days. (Clears throat)

1944
01:44:42,583 --> 01:44:44,708
Let's see now. Let's…

1945
01:44:45,875 --> 01:44:46,875
(groans)

1946
01:44:48,000 --> 01:44:49,250
Okay.

1947
01:44:50,750 --> 01:44:53,083
This might get unpleasant.

1948
01:44:53,167 --> 01:44:54,792
I mean, more unpleasant.

1949
01:44:55,333 --> 01:44:57,292
- (squeaks)
- (liquid draining)

1950
01:45:04,208 --> 01:45:06,208
(dramatic sinister music plays)

1951
01:45:30,333 --> 01:45:31,417
Dr. Nat.

1952
01:45:32,667 --> 01:45:35,500
In the flesh. Yeah… Or, what's left of it.

1953
01:45:38,292 --> 01:45:39,292
(clears throat)

1954
01:45:40,250 --> 01:45:41,375
(Benoit exhales)

1955
01:46:06,458 --> 01:46:08,417
(line ringing)

1956
01:46:08,500 --> 01:46:10,500
Geraldine, it's… it's Blanc. Um…

1957
01:46:11,625 --> 01:46:13,792
Yeah, he's standing right here.

1958
01:46:13,875 --> 01:46:15,375
(hesitates) Listen to me.

1959
01:46:15,458 --> 01:46:17,625
You're gonna wanna come
to Dr. Nat's house.

1960
01:46:17,708 --> 01:46:21,125
(breathing heavily)
There's a body. Or two.

1961
01:46:22,250 --> 01:46:23,667
It's all here.

1962
01:46:24,167 --> 01:46:27,042
- Yes, yeah. It's… it's finished, yeah.
- (stair creaks)

1963
01:46:28,167 --> 01:46:29,667
(sighs) I'll call you back.

1964
01:46:30,958 --> 01:46:32,792
Father Jud. Wait, wait.

1965
01:46:32,875 --> 01:46:35,000
I killed Samson. I have to do this.

1966
01:46:35,625 --> 01:46:38,250
I have to do it of my own free will
or it won't mean anything.

1967
01:46:53,792 --> 01:46:57,917
(female officer over radio) <i>Plate check.</i>
<i>Copy that. Any available units to respond…</i>

1968
01:46:58,000 --> 01:47:00,125
Would you call Geraldine for me, please?

1969
01:47:00,625 --> 01:47:03,458
Say Father Jud's returned to his church
and he's ready to confess.

1970
01:47:04,750 --> 01:47:06,250
(door creaking)

1971
01:47:06,333 --> 01:47:07,458
(door thuds)

1972
01:47:20,042 --> 01:47:22,750
Father Jud.
I'm here to arrest you for the murder

1973
01:47:22,833 --> 01:47:25,083
of Monsignor Jefferson Wicks
and Samson Holt.

1974
01:47:25,167 --> 01:47:29,333
And you're a person of interest
in the death of Dr. Nathaniel Sharp.

1975
01:47:29,417 --> 01:47:30,833
(splutters) Nat is dead?

1976
01:47:32,042 --> 01:47:33,333
Murdered in his home.

1977
01:47:34,333 --> 01:47:36,833
We also recovered Wicks' body. It's over.

1978
01:47:37,333 --> 01:47:40,458
Anything you say
can be used against you in a court of law.

1979
01:47:40,542 --> 01:47:43,167
But if you'd like to confess to anything,

1980
01:47:43,250 --> 01:47:46,083
this seems like
a pretty great place to do it.

1981
01:47:48,250 --> 01:47:49,333
Yeah.

1982
01:47:52,375 --> 01:47:54,125
Years ago,

1983
01:47:54,208 --> 01:47:56,625
I murdered a man in a boxing ring.

1984
01:47:58,333 --> 01:48:00,375
I killed him with hate in my heart.

1985
01:48:02,500 --> 01:48:05,917
Last night, that same sin rose in me
and in a moment of

1986
01:48:06,875 --> 01:48:09,042
fear and rage, I...

1987
01:48:09,125 --> 01:48:11,417
("Overture" from
The Phantom Of The Opera playing)

1988
01:48:13,500 --> 01:48:17,542
I'm sorry, that was dramatic,
but I needed you to stop talking.

1989
01:48:17,625 --> 01:48:19,875
- No. Father Jud...
- I was about to explain to everyone…

1990
01:48:19,958 --> 01:48:21,708
- Sit down and listen.
- Stop talking.

1991
01:48:21,792 --> 01:48:24,750
Please, let him. You were continuing…
Continue, you said last night…

1992
01:48:24,833 --> 01:48:27,167
- In a moment of fear and rage…
- I was about to do it…

1993
01:48:27,250 --> 01:48:30,333
(dramatically) You shall not silence
the voice of the Lord!

1994
01:48:30,417 --> 01:48:35,333
But sit now and behold the wickedness
and shame of the guilty

1995
01:48:35,417 --> 01:48:38,250
laid bare before you all!

1996
01:48:51,000 --> 01:48:54,125
- (whispering) What are you doing?
- (clears throat)

1997
01:48:55,833 --> 01:48:57,125
(smacks lips)

1998
01:48:57,208 --> 01:49:00,417
Let us begin with Wicks' murder.

1999
01:49:00,500 --> 01:49:03,333
Right here on Good Friday.

2000
01:49:04,042 --> 01:49:05,875
The impossible crime.

2001
01:49:07,250 --> 01:49:09,875
And, Geraldine,
you were correct in your deduction.

2002
01:49:09,958 --> 01:49:14,125
When Monsignor Wicks collapsed
in that closet space, he wasn't dead.

2003
01:49:14,208 --> 01:49:16,333
He wasn't even stabbed, not yet.

2004
01:49:17,333 --> 01:49:20,750
The flask he kept stashed
in the breaker box

2005
01:49:20,833 --> 01:49:24,542
<i>was spiked
with a very powerful tranquilizer.</i>

2006
01:49:24,625 --> 01:49:26,417
- (suspenseful music plays)
<i>- He drank from it.</i>

2007
01:49:26,500 --> 01:49:28,375
Fortified himself.

2008
01:49:28,458 --> 01:49:31,667
<i>And within minutes,
fell to the floor, unconscious.</i>

2009
01:49:31,750 --> 01:49:34,708
- (flask clangs)
- (Benoit) <i>The clanky clunk.</i>

2010
01:49:34,792 --> 01:49:36,625
Leaving him defenseless

2011
01:49:36,708 --> 01:49:40,125
and giving the killer
their chance to enter the closet

2012
01:49:40,708 --> 01:49:42,375
and deliver the deadly blow.

2013
01:49:43,000 --> 01:49:44,208
I… I said that already.

2014
01:49:44,792 --> 01:49:45,625
Father Jud.

2015
01:49:45,708 --> 01:49:48,542
No. The knife was in his back
when I found him.

2016
01:49:48,625 --> 01:49:50,208
There's something in his back.

2017
01:49:50,292 --> 01:49:53,333
So how? When? It's impossible. I saw.

2018
01:49:53,417 --> 01:49:54,875
What did you see?

2019
01:49:56,083 --> 01:49:57,500
The red devil head.

2020
01:49:57,583 --> 01:50:00,792
<i>Blood you assumed was Wicks'.</i>

2021
01:50:00,875 --> 01:50:03,125
Now, I showed you
the answer to this, did you see?

2022
01:50:04,375 --> 01:50:05,667
Il Diavolo.

2023
01:50:05,750 --> 01:50:07,333
The pizza bar. The photograph.

2024
01:50:08,667 --> 01:50:10,667
<i>You thought you saw,</i>

2025
01:50:11,208 --> 01:50:13,125
<i>but that wasn't it, no.</i>

2026
01:50:13,208 --> 01:50:15,417
<i>It was a second identical lamp.</i>

2027
01:50:15,500 --> 01:50:18,375
<i>A second identical devil head.</i>

2028
01:50:19,708 --> 01:50:20,792
Yeah.

2029
01:50:23,792 --> 01:50:25,417
<i>And it was also missing.</i>

2030
01:50:26,042 --> 01:50:27,458
Two devils.

2031
01:50:27,542 --> 01:50:28,875
(Benoit) Yes.

2032
01:50:28,958 --> 01:50:30,167
Why two?

2033
01:50:31,042 --> 01:50:32,667
And why painted red?

2034
01:50:32,750 --> 01:50:34,167
It wasn't red though. It's red now.

2035
01:50:34,250 --> 01:50:37,000
(Benoit) The same red
as the Good Friday vestments.

2036
01:50:37,083 --> 01:50:38,917
The same exact red

2037
01:50:39,000 --> 01:50:42,083
as the mysterious thread
found in the closet.

2038
01:50:42,792 --> 01:50:46,583
<i>Because the second devil head
was there all the time.</i>

2039
01:50:46,667 --> 01:50:49,000
<i>Sewn to the back of his vestments.</i>

2040
01:50:49,083 --> 01:50:50,375
Hollow, light,

2041
01:50:50,458 --> 01:50:52,542
and filled with a small squib of blood

2042
01:50:53,125 --> 01:50:56,042
<i>- triggered by an RF remote.</i>
- (static crackles)

2043
01:50:57,000 --> 01:51:00,208
(Benoit) <i>Set off</i>
<i>at the exact right moment.</i>

2044
01:51:00,292 --> 01:51:01,292
(Jud) Monsignor?

2045
01:51:02,500 --> 01:51:03,500
The doctor.

2046
01:51:05,125 --> 01:51:06,417
<i>A voice of authority</i>

2047
01:51:06,500 --> 01:51:10,042
<i>who can wait for the discovery he needs
before taking charge.</i>

2048
01:51:10,125 --> 01:51:11,333
There's something in his back.

2049
01:51:11,417 --> 01:51:13,042
Wait. Don't touch it.

2050
01:51:15,333 --> 01:51:17,750
A moment of distraction presents itself.

2051
01:51:17,833 --> 01:51:19,167
(imperceptible)

2052
01:51:20,333 --> 01:51:22,333
<i>And the deed is quickly done.</i>

2053
01:51:23,833 --> 01:51:25,083
<i>His final task,</i>

2054
01:51:25,167 --> 01:51:29,500
<i>to remove the incriminating
drug-laced flask.</i>

2055
01:51:29,583 --> 01:51:32,417
<i>But where was it? It was gone.</i>

2056
01:51:33,542 --> 01:51:35,750
The one hiccup in his plan.

2057
01:51:35,833 --> 01:51:39,708
The result of a moment
of foolish grace by Father Jud

2058
01:51:40,292 --> 01:51:44,833
<i>who concealed the flask
to hide Wicks' drinking</i>

2059
01:51:44,917 --> 01:51:47,750
<i>and returned later to retrieve it.</i>

2060
01:51:50,083 --> 01:51:51,292
My God.

2061
01:51:51,792 --> 01:51:52,958
Nat.

2062
01:51:53,042 --> 01:51:54,250
Why?

2063
01:51:54,750 --> 01:51:57,000
(Vera) Wicks was going to scorch
the earth.

2064
01:51:57,083 --> 01:51:58,708
He was going to ruin him.

2065
01:51:58,792 --> 01:52:01,625
No. The bigger why.
The why that brought you here.

2066
01:52:01,708 --> 01:52:04,125
Why do all this insane, elaborate stuff?

2067
01:52:04,208 --> 01:52:07,083
The theatricality? The impossible crime.

2068
01:52:07,167 --> 01:52:08,375
Why?

2069
01:52:09,042 --> 01:52:10,250
Indeed.

2070
01:52:10,333 --> 01:52:12,833
Okay, so… if Dr. Nat killed Wicks,

2071
01:52:13,375 --> 01:52:14,375
who killed Nat?

2072
01:52:14,458 --> 01:52:16,292
Well, now we get to it.

2073
01:52:17,000 --> 01:52:19,750
Not some fiddly locked-door mystery

2074
01:52:19,833 --> 01:52:23,208
with devices and clues,

2075
01:52:23,292 --> 01:52:26,708
but a much, much larger scheme.

2076
01:52:26,792 --> 01:52:31,875
One whose roots
run to the bedrock of this church.

2077
01:52:31,958 --> 01:52:33,708
And one which draws me,

2078
01:52:33,792 --> 01:52:37,042
an unbeliever in every sense of the word,

2079
01:52:37,125 --> 01:52:40,042
into the realm of belief.

2080
01:52:41,667 --> 01:52:43,500
To understand this case,

2081
01:52:44,542 --> 01:52:48,625
I had to look at the myth
that was being constructed.

2082
01:52:48,708 --> 01:52:51,542
Not to solve whether it was real or not,

2083
01:52:51,625 --> 01:52:54,042
but to feel in my soul

2084
01:52:54,125 --> 01:52:57,250
the essence of that
which it strove to convey.

2085
01:53:00,542 --> 01:53:01,958
A holy priest.

2086
01:53:02,708 --> 01:53:08,125
Struck down by no man,
but by the hand of Satan himself.

2087
01:53:08,208 --> 01:53:11,625
Laid to rest
in the sealed tomb of his father,

2088
01:53:12,208 --> 01:53:13,625
but then risen

2089
01:53:14,333 --> 01:53:15,958
by the will of God.

2090
01:53:16,042 --> 01:53:18,042
Risen as something new.

2091
01:53:18,125 --> 01:53:20,125
No longer a fallible man,

2092
01:53:20,208 --> 01:53:24,042
but now a symbol
of the Lord's power over death.

2093
01:53:26,000 --> 01:53:27,625
His justice for the holy.

2094
01:53:28,125 --> 01:53:30,375
His vengeance for the wicked.

2095
01:53:33,167 --> 01:53:37,000
Okay. And now, what really happened?

2096
01:53:37,083 --> 01:53:39,083
- Yes. Yes.
- (intriguing music plays)

2097
01:53:39,167 --> 01:53:43,000
It is time to break this tawdry facade

2098
01:53:43,083 --> 01:53:47,083
of miracles and resurrections
and reveal what really happened.

2099
01:53:47,167 --> 01:53:49,583
It is time for Benoit Blanc's

2100
01:53:49,667 --> 01:53:52,750
final checkmate
over the mysteries of faith!

2101
01:54:06,208 --> 01:54:07,333
(exhales heavily)

2102
01:54:07,417 --> 01:54:09,583
(solemn string music plays)

2103
01:54:18,750 --> 01:54:19,750
(sighs softly)

2104
01:54:21,292 --> 01:54:23,292
Blanc, are you… Are you okay?

2105
01:54:25,417 --> 01:54:26,625
Damascus.

2106
01:54:27,667 --> 01:54:28,875
Damascus?

2107
01:54:30,250 --> 01:54:33,292
Like… a road to Damascus thing?

2108
01:54:33,375 --> 01:54:35,250
Yes, yes, Damascus.

2109
01:54:38,792 --> 01:54:40,417
Shit. (Sighs)

2110
01:54:41,292 --> 01:54:42,375
Blanc?

2111
01:54:43,000 --> 01:54:44,083
(inhales, clicks tongue)

2112
01:54:44,167 --> 01:54:45,167
(exhales)

2113
01:54:58,917 --> 01:55:00,542
I cannot solve this case.

2114
01:55:04,500 --> 01:55:05,500
What?

2115
01:55:06,583 --> 01:55:09,375
Are you saying that
your conclusion, Benoit Blanc,

2116
01:55:09,458 --> 01:55:12,417
is that Monsignor Wicks
rose from the dead?

2117
01:55:12,500 --> 01:55:13,917
That it was a miracle?

2118
01:55:14,000 --> 01:55:18,125
I'm saying I cannot solve this case.

2119
01:55:18,208 --> 01:55:19,583
(cell phone clicks)

2120
01:55:19,667 --> 01:55:20,750
That works.

2121
01:55:21,250 --> 01:55:22,250
Thank you.

2122
01:55:24,458 --> 01:55:25,542
(Jud) Blanc?

2123
01:55:26,250 --> 01:55:28,667
If you know what really happened,
you should tell everyone.

2124
01:55:28,750 --> 01:55:32,458
Is this you sparing our faith
or being respectful or something?

2125
01:55:32,542 --> 01:55:34,750
Because we deserve the truth.

2126
01:55:34,833 --> 01:55:36,250
It is not.

2127
01:55:36,333 --> 01:55:37,542
(breath shaking)

2128
01:55:37,625 --> 01:55:39,250
I need the truth.

2129
01:55:40,542 --> 01:55:42,833
(scoffs) Can't you just

2130
01:55:42,917 --> 01:55:45,792
give us the answer?
Isn't that what all this is for?

2131
01:55:48,583 --> 01:55:51,542
And would you consider blurbing my book?

2132
01:55:51,625 --> 01:55:53,333
(hesitates) No.

2133
01:55:53,958 --> 01:55:56,500
(Geraldine) Okay. All right.
Show's over. Everyone out.

2134
01:55:57,333 --> 01:55:59,750
Out. Out.

2135
01:56:00,458 --> 01:56:02,167
(officer 1) Yeah, can you stand back, sir?

2136
01:56:02,250 --> 01:56:03,375
(indistinct chatter)

2137
01:56:03,458 --> 01:56:05,083
(officer 2) Okay, can we keep them back…

2138
01:56:05,167 --> 01:56:06,667
(mellow intriguing music plays)

2139
01:56:06,750 --> 01:56:09,583
I add another chapter
and then we're… we're ready.

2140
01:56:09,667 --> 01:56:12,000
We're ready to publish. Trust me, Alan.

2141
01:56:12,083 --> 01:56:14,708
Call Random House, everybody.
It's gonna be huge!

2142
01:56:17,833 --> 01:56:21,708
What we've witnessed is a miracle
confirmed by Benoit Blanc himself.

2143
01:56:21,792 --> 01:56:25,125
The world will know
what happened today here at Chimney Rock.

2144
01:56:25,208 --> 01:56:29,208
You can find out yourself.
Follow my YouTube channel @CyDraven…

2145
01:56:29,292 --> 01:56:30,500
What a mess.

2146
01:56:32,000 --> 01:56:34,417
I assume they'll arrest Father Jud now.

2147
01:56:35,000 --> 01:56:36,083
Yes.

2148
01:56:37,042 --> 01:56:38,667
I suppose they will.

2149
01:56:44,833 --> 01:56:46,333
What the hell was that?

2150
01:56:46,875 --> 01:56:48,875
Road to Damascus.

2151
01:56:49,583 --> 01:56:52,000
Scales fell from my eyes.

2152
01:56:52,083 --> 01:56:53,917
So what? Facts, schmacks?

2153
01:56:54,000 --> 01:56:56,542
You believe in God
and all this <i>mishegoss </i>is real?

2154
01:56:56,625 --> 01:56:58,458
No, no. God is a fiction.

2155
01:56:58,542 --> 01:57:00,542
My revelation came from…

2156
01:57:01,625 --> 01:57:03,042
From Father Jud.

2157
01:57:04,500 --> 01:57:06,917
- His example to have grace.
- (door opens)

2158
01:57:09,583 --> 01:57:11,417
Grace for my enemy.

2159
01:57:15,167 --> 01:57:16,542
Grace for the broken.

2160
01:57:19,000 --> 01:57:20,625
Grace for those who

2161
01:57:21,417 --> 01:57:22,542
deserve it the least.

2162
01:57:24,625 --> 01:57:26,042
But who need it the most.

2163
01:57:28,542 --> 01:57:30,458
(breathing shakily)

2164
01:57:31,292 --> 01:57:32,500
For the guilty.

2165
01:57:33,083 --> 01:57:34,167
(Martha) Mr. Blanc.

2166
01:57:34,833 --> 01:57:36,458
You know the truth.

2167
01:57:37,042 --> 01:57:39,042
I do, yes.

2168
01:57:40,583 --> 01:57:43,917
And you made yourself the fool just now.

2169
01:57:44,000 --> 01:57:46,625
So that you could do this
of your own free will.

2170
01:57:47,917 --> 01:57:50,417
And now you better do it. Quickly.

2171
01:57:50,500 --> 01:57:51,708
Thank you.

2172
01:57:55,583 --> 01:57:57,000
Father Jud.

2173
01:57:57,500 --> 01:57:59,500
(breathing shakily)

2174
01:58:04,000 --> 01:58:05,125
(softly) What do I do?

2175
01:58:05,208 --> 01:58:07,042
What you were born to do.

2176
01:58:07,125 --> 01:58:08,542
Be her priest.

2177
01:58:09,042 --> 01:58:10,458
Take her confession.

2178
01:58:19,125 --> 01:58:21,125
Bless me, Father, for I have sinned.

2179
01:58:21,208 --> 01:58:23,417
It is a week since my last confession.

2180
01:58:27,917 --> 01:58:32,750
I told myself it started with pure intent.

2181
01:58:34,125 --> 01:58:35,542
But the truth is

2182
01:58:36,375 --> 01:58:39,458
it started with a lie.

2183
01:58:40,417 --> 01:58:41,500
Prentice.

2184
01:58:41,583 --> 01:58:42,958
(intriguing string music plays)

2185
01:58:43,042 --> 01:58:44,042
(Martha) <i>Prentice.</i>

2186
01:58:45,625 --> 01:58:48,625
<i>I saw him take his final communion.</i>

2187
01:58:52,500 --> 01:58:54,625
This is Eve's Apple, Martha.

2188
01:58:55,208 --> 01:58:57,417
My entire cursed fortune.

2189
01:58:57,917 --> 01:59:00,333
All the sin in the world.

2190
01:59:00,417 --> 01:59:02,333
All that Eve hungers for.

2191
01:59:03,000 --> 01:59:04,625
I have trapped it.

2192
01:59:05,208 --> 01:59:08,625
It shall never again
be plucked by evil hands.

2193
01:59:09,417 --> 01:59:11,333
The body of Christ.

2194
01:59:12,708 --> 01:59:14,125
(music turns ominous)

2195
01:59:14,208 --> 01:59:15,250
(groaning)

2196
01:59:16,375 --> 01:59:17,833
(Prentice gulps, groans)

2197
01:59:19,917 --> 01:59:21,458
(exhales)

2198
01:59:24,458 --> 01:59:27,875
(Martha) <i>He took the jewel to his grave.</i>

2199
01:59:27,958 --> 01:59:29,958
(suspenseful music plays)

2200
01:59:30,625 --> 01:59:35,292
<i>I swore that I would
protect this great secret.</i>

2201
01:59:36,708 --> 01:59:40,625
<i>But Grace, she discovered that
he had bought the diamond.</i>

2202
01:59:40,708 --> 01:59:42,000
I don't know how.

2203
01:59:42,083 --> 01:59:43,917
She knew her fancy brands.

2204
01:59:45,167 --> 01:59:48,500
<i>What would come
in a custom-made Fabergé box,</i>

2205
01:59:48,583 --> 01:59:50,750
<i>itself worth maybe $20,000?</i>

2206
01:59:50,833 --> 01:59:54,917
<i>Not a trinket or a plastic Jesus, no.</i>

2207
01:59:55,000 --> 01:59:57,167
<i>Something facet-cut, worth a fortune.</i>

2208
01:59:58,250 --> 01:59:59,333
<i>A jewel.</i>

2209
01:59:59,417 --> 02:00:02,125
But she didn't know where he hid it.

2210
02:00:02,208 --> 02:00:03,708
So that night…

2211
02:00:06,167 --> 02:00:08,292
<i>She didn't desecrate the church in anger.</i>

2212
02:00:08,875 --> 02:00:11,917
(Benoit) <i>No, she was looking for</i>
<i>the hidden jewel.</i>

2213
02:00:12,000 --> 02:00:15,500
- (Grace sobbing)
- (Benoit) <i>A dark life of desperation.</i>

2214
02:00:16,042 --> 02:00:19,125
<i>A prisoner to shame and judgment.</i>

2215
02:00:19,625 --> 02:00:21,625
<i>It was her one way out.</i>

2216
02:00:22,625 --> 02:00:24,042
That poor girl.

2217
02:00:25,583 --> 02:00:27,417
Martha, what did you say to her?

2218
02:00:29,542 --> 02:00:31,375
I know where he hid it.

2219
02:00:31,458 --> 02:00:33,500
And you'll never find it.

2220
02:00:33,583 --> 02:00:35,000
You harlot whore.

2221
02:00:40,208 --> 02:00:42,125
- (yells) Where is it?
- (screams)

2222
02:00:42,208 --> 02:00:44,750
- (yelling)
- (giggling)

2223
02:00:44,833 --> 02:00:47,208
Where is it, you little shit?

2224
02:00:48,208 --> 02:00:51,292
I kept the secret of Eve's Apple

2225
02:00:51,375 --> 02:00:55,958
locked in my heart for 60 years.

2226
02:00:57,125 --> 02:00:59,750
My terrible burden.

2227
02:01:00,958 --> 02:01:01,833
Until…

2228
02:01:01,917 --> 02:01:03,167
Until…

2229
02:01:03,250 --> 02:01:05,083
(melancholic music plays)

2230
02:01:05,167 --> 02:01:07,250
I challenged you to confess it.

2231
02:01:07,333 --> 02:01:10,708
- (imperceptible)
- (Martha) <i>With defiant pride,</i>

2232
02:01:11,750 --> 02:01:13,167
<i>I confessed.</i>

2233
02:01:14,000 --> 02:01:16,167
(panting)

2234
02:01:16,750 --> 02:01:18,375
To the wrong priest.

2235
02:01:19,917 --> 02:01:21,250
(breath trembles)

2236
02:01:22,583 --> 02:01:24,625
Time is of the essence now.

2237
02:01:24,708 --> 02:01:26,708
Last Sunday, in the rectory,

2238
02:01:26,792 --> 02:01:29,958
<i>Vera confronted Wicks
and you learned about Cy.</i>

2239
02:01:30,042 --> 02:01:33,000
I could accept that he had strayed.

2240
02:01:33,083 --> 02:01:36,792
- (imperceptible)
<i>- But as he spoke, something became clear.</i>

2241
02:01:37,708 --> 02:01:39,917
<i>This was something much bigger.</i>

2242
02:01:40,417 --> 02:01:44,833
<i>He was embracing that terrible boy.</i>

2243
02:01:46,542 --> 02:01:48,667
<i>That's when I suspected.</i>

2244
02:01:48,750 --> 02:01:51,125
So you call the construction company.

2245
02:01:51,208 --> 02:01:52,625
Thank you, James.

2246
02:01:54,875 --> 02:01:56,083
(Martha) <i>And I was certain.</i>

2247
02:01:57,000 --> 02:02:00,417
<i>He had ordered the equipment
to open the crypt</i>

2248
02:02:00,500 --> 02:02:06,333
<i>to steal the diamond
for his own greed and lust for power.</i>

2249
02:02:06,417 --> 02:02:10,875
<i>The corrupting sin
of Eve's Apple would be unearthed</i>

2250
02:02:11,542 --> 02:02:13,958
<i>and this church would fall</i>

2251
02:02:14,042 --> 02:02:18,667
<i>because of everything
Prentice had warned me about.</i>

2252
02:02:18,750 --> 02:02:20,167
<i>I had failed him.</i>

2253
02:02:22,750 --> 02:02:23,958
All my life,

2254
02:02:24,583 --> 02:02:27,917
I was not the bad one. I was the good one.

2255
02:02:28,500 --> 02:02:30,083
The faithful one.

2256
02:02:30,167 --> 02:02:32,792
Serving and protecting the church.

2257
02:02:33,417 --> 02:02:36,500
If I failed in that, what is my life?

2258
02:02:36,583 --> 02:02:37,667
I understand.

2259
02:02:37,750 --> 02:02:40,375
My sole purpose

2260
02:02:40,458 --> 02:02:41,875
and I failed.

2261
02:02:42,958 --> 02:02:44,167
Unless…

2262
02:02:45,375 --> 02:02:46,750
(breath trembles)

2263
02:02:48,167 --> 02:02:49,167
Unless…

2264
02:02:51,833 --> 02:02:55,583
<i>Unless I could…
I could steal the jewel first</i>

2265
02:02:55,667 --> 02:02:57,417
<i>and get rid of it forever.</i>

2266
02:02:58,417 --> 02:02:59,833
<i>And with the same stroke,</i>

2267
02:02:59,917 --> 02:03:04,167
<i>raise Wicks up
as a miraculous risen saint.</i>

2268
02:03:04,250 --> 02:03:07,667
<i>Not a fallible man, but a symbol</i>

2269
02:03:08,500 --> 02:03:10,500
<i>that would save my church.</i>

2270
02:03:11,667 --> 02:03:14,208
<i>All it would take is a miracle.</i>

2271
02:03:15,583 --> 02:03:17,417
So I formed my plan.

2272
02:03:18,417 --> 02:03:22,500
Wicks' death must be a holy mystery.

2273
02:03:23,292 --> 02:03:26,375
Unsolvable and divine.

2274
02:03:27,375 --> 02:03:29,125
But you couldn't do it alone.

2275
02:03:29,833 --> 02:03:30,917
No.

2276
02:03:32,458 --> 02:03:34,083
<i>A weak man, I thought.</i>

2277
02:03:34,667 --> 02:03:35,875
<i>Desperate.</i>

2278
02:03:35,958 --> 02:03:38,708
<i>Someone who would fall in line
to save the church</i>

2279
02:03:38,792 --> 02:03:41,375
<i>and stay in line to cover his shame.</i>

2280
02:03:41,958 --> 02:03:45,917
And who had access
to medical-grade tranquilizers.

2281
02:03:46,000 --> 02:03:48,042
Yes. And that.

2282
02:03:51,458 --> 02:03:54,417
<i>It all went according to plan.</i>

2283
02:03:56,000 --> 02:03:58,083
<i>Oh, God. </i>(Breathing heavily)

2284
02:03:58,167 --> 02:03:59,250
<i>My vanity.</i>

2285
02:03:59,333 --> 02:04:00,750
So wicked.

2286
02:04:01,292 --> 02:04:02,417
(Jud) Martha.

2287
02:04:03,042 --> 02:04:05,500
I understand, I promise, I do.

2288
02:04:06,083 --> 02:04:07,917
Keep going. I'm here.

2289
02:04:08,000 --> 02:04:10,375
(Martha) I didn't reckon the cost.

2290
02:04:11,458 --> 02:04:13,292
Forgive me, Samson.

2291
02:04:13,833 --> 02:04:16,250
Strong Samson, faithful Samson.

2292
02:04:16,333 --> 02:04:18,875
Samson. Who made the coffins.

2293
02:04:21,542 --> 02:04:23,833
(grunts) Shit.

2294
02:04:24,625 --> 02:04:26,042
(Martha) You will rise again.

2295
02:04:27,000 --> 02:04:28,833
It will be okay.

2296
02:04:28,917 --> 02:04:30,542
You will rise again.

2297
02:04:31,125 --> 02:04:33,375
It will be okay. (Exhales)

2298
02:04:33,458 --> 02:04:35,333
(melancholic music plays)

2299
02:04:35,417 --> 02:04:36,625
I promise.

2300
02:04:37,333 --> 02:04:40,542
<i>He didn't understand why we were doing it.</i>

2301
02:04:40,625 --> 02:04:43,458
Anything for you, my angel.

2302
02:04:44,208 --> 02:04:45,375
(Martha) <i>But he trusted me.</i>

2303
02:04:45,875 --> 02:04:47,708
<i>Because he loved me.</i>

2304
02:04:48,375 --> 02:04:50,500
Oh, Lord. (Sobs)

2305
02:04:55,250 --> 02:04:57,083
How did it go so wrong?

2306
02:04:57,667 --> 02:04:59,667
(thunder crashing)

2307
02:04:59,750 --> 02:05:01,750
(Martha) <i>It was supposed to be so simple.</i>

2308
02:05:01,833 --> 02:05:03,792
<i>The doctor gives the signal.</i>

2309
02:05:03,875 --> 02:05:05,000
(cell phone chimes)

2310
02:05:16,208 --> 02:05:18,625
(Martha) <i>Samson retrieves the jewel.</i>

2311
02:05:19,875 --> 02:05:22,708
<i>The Lazarus door serves its purpose.</i>

2312
02:05:25,542 --> 02:05:26,792
(beeps)

2313
02:05:26,875 --> 02:05:30,167
<i>All caught on camera the way we planned.</i>

2314
02:05:30,792 --> 02:05:33,583
<i>Dr. Nat would drive off
with Wicks' body in his truck</i>

2315
02:05:34,500 --> 02:05:37,833
<i>and dispose of it
in that nasty gook in his cellar.</i>

2316
02:05:37,917 --> 02:05:42,000
<i>And the next day, Samson would
tell the tale of the risen saint</i>

2317
02:05:42,083 --> 02:05:46,083
<i>and his word of blessing
to his faithful groundskeeper</i>

2318
02:05:46,167 --> 02:05:49,000
<i>before ascending back into heaven.</i>

2319
02:05:49,667 --> 02:05:51,083
<i>A miracle.</i>

2320
02:05:51,667 --> 02:05:53,500
<i>It would have been perfect.</i>

2321
02:05:55,417 --> 02:05:57,542
I wasn't supposed to be there.

2322
02:05:57,625 --> 02:05:59,667
You most certainly were not.

2323
02:06:00,458 --> 02:06:01,542
(Benoit) Did you know

2324
02:06:01,625 --> 02:06:04,708
what had happened
when you found Samson's body?

2325
02:06:04,792 --> 02:06:06,500
I had an idea.

2326
02:06:06,583 --> 02:06:08,583
(sobbing) No, no!

2327
02:06:09,250 --> 02:06:11,083
But I had to be sure.

2328
02:06:14,542 --> 02:06:15,750
(Nat) Praise be.

2329
02:06:16,250 --> 02:06:17,458
It's accomplished.

2330
02:06:35,958 --> 02:06:39,292
- (clatters)
- Oh. Oh. Oh.

2331
02:06:42,208 --> 02:06:44,208
(Martha) <i>Then he told me the fairy tale</i>

2332
02:06:44,292 --> 02:06:47,292
<i>of how everything
had gone according to plan.</i>

2333
02:06:48,750 --> 02:06:52,208
<i>It was only then that I told him
I'd been to the crypt.</i>

2334
02:06:54,000 --> 02:06:56,667
<i>- And I knew he was lying.</i>
- (gulps)

2335
02:06:58,417 --> 02:07:00,542
(Martha) <i>And then he told me the truth.</i>

2336
02:07:01,500 --> 02:07:03,250
- (thunder rumbling)
- (yelps, groans)

2337
02:07:05,333 --> 02:07:07,750
Shit. We can't let him see us.

2338
02:07:08,792 --> 02:07:10,375
(Jud pants, groans)

2339
02:07:12,250 --> 02:07:13,458
(gasps softly)

2340
02:07:16,333 --> 02:07:17,542
(Nat) Jesus.

2341
02:07:20,542 --> 02:07:22,167
(Martha) <i>My second mistake.</i>

2342
02:07:22,667 --> 02:07:27,292
<i>Underestimating the temptation
of Eve's Apple.</i>

2343
02:07:28,542 --> 02:07:33,000
<i>Our agreed mission was to destroy it
or throw it in the sea.</i>

2344
02:07:33,083 --> 02:07:37,500
<i>But all this power will I give thee.</i>

2345
02:07:38,417 --> 02:07:41,542
<i>Christ himself could resist temptation,</i>

2346
02:07:41,625 --> 02:07:44,833
<i>but this desperate little man,</i>

2347
02:07:45,333 --> 02:07:48,542
<i>all that stood in his way
was Samson and I.</i>

2348
02:07:49,375 --> 02:07:51,375
<i>Now, here was his opportunity.</i>

2349
02:07:52,250 --> 02:07:55,500
To remove his obstacles.

2350
02:07:55,583 --> 02:07:56,500
(thunder crashes)

2351
02:07:56,583 --> 02:08:00,583
Frame a young priest with a violent past

2352
02:08:00,667 --> 02:08:02,500
and keep the jewel.

2353
02:08:04,458 --> 02:08:05,292
He took it.

2354
02:08:05,375 --> 02:08:06,708
(yells)

2355
02:08:09,833 --> 02:08:13,792
<i>Then all that remained in his way was me.</i>

2356
02:08:13,875 --> 02:08:14,708
(imperceptible)

2357
02:08:14,792 --> 02:08:19,292
<i>He had poisoned my coffee
with a lethal dose of pentobarbital.</i>

2358
02:08:20,208 --> 02:08:22,833
<i>No remedy once ingested.</i>

2359
02:08:23,583 --> 02:08:24,917
<i>Mm, painless.</i>

2360
02:08:25,000 --> 02:08:27,833
<i>A little numbness in the lips.</i>

2361
02:08:28,500 --> 02:08:31,583
<i>Then in ten minutes,
time for your final prayer.</i>

2362
02:08:32,417 --> 02:08:35,667
<i>Then he begged me to understand
why he was doing all this.</i>

2363
02:08:35,750 --> 02:08:39,208
<i>That the money would lure back
his harpy wife,</i>

2364
02:08:39,292 --> 02:08:41,125
<i>blah, blah, blah.</i>

2365
02:08:41,833 --> 02:08:44,083
<i>I told him I understood.</i>

2366
02:08:45,417 --> 02:08:47,417
<i>I understood why he did it.</i>

2367
02:08:48,708 --> 02:08:49,792
- (clatters)
- Oh.

2368
02:08:51,875 --> 02:08:54,500
(Martha) <i>I had understood it all.</i>

2369
02:09:14,708 --> 02:09:16,708
(Martha) <i>These things I did with</i>

2370
02:09:17,458 --> 02:09:20,083
<i>hatred in my heart.</i>

2371
02:09:25,167 --> 02:09:27,583
(Martha) <i>Vengeance is mine, said the Lord.</i>

2372
02:09:33,125 --> 02:09:36,625
<i>And that is the story
the crime scene will tell the world, but…</i>

2373
02:09:37,208 --> 02:09:39,500
- (squeaks)
- (liquid sloshing)

2374
02:09:39,583 --> 02:09:41,417
(Martha) <i>…inside my heart,</i>

2375
02:09:42,167 --> 02:09:43,375
<i>I know.</i>

2376
02:09:44,375 --> 02:09:45,375
(switch clicks)

2377
02:09:47,458 --> 02:09:49,083
Vengeance is mine.

2378
02:09:52,917 --> 02:09:56,500
These sins I confess to you, Father.

2379
02:09:56,583 --> 02:09:59,792
(breathing heavily) I have lied,
I have killed,

2380
02:10:00,500 --> 02:10:01,708
and now

2381
02:10:02,708 --> 02:10:05,333
I have topped it all off
with a real doozy.

2382
02:10:05,417 --> 02:10:07,542
(breathing heavily)

2383
02:10:09,958 --> 02:10:11,208
(gasps)

2384
02:10:13,000 --> 02:10:14,625
Father. Quickly now, quickly.

2385
02:10:14,708 --> 02:10:16,000
(hesitates) What's happening?

2386
02:10:16,083 --> 02:10:18,125
I knew when I saw her lips…

2387
02:10:20,167 --> 02:10:21,875
<i>It was already too late.</i>

2388
02:10:21,958 --> 02:10:22,958
(sighs)

2389
02:10:23,708 --> 02:10:25,708
She's taken the pentobarbital.

2390
02:10:25,792 --> 02:10:28,708
- Oh. Oh, God. Call the ambulance now!
- On it!

2391
02:10:28,792 --> 02:10:31,208
There might be a poison kit
in the prowler!

2392
02:10:38,750 --> 02:10:40,917
(labored breathing)

2393
02:10:42,708 --> 02:10:44,333
Forgive me, Father,

2394
02:10:45,542 --> 02:10:46,958
for all you have endured.

2395
02:10:48,625 --> 02:10:53,458
Forgive me, Lord, for…
for Wicks and Nat and…

2396
02:10:55,667 --> 02:10:56,875
Samson.

2397
02:10:57,500 --> 02:10:59,125
(sobs) My sweet Samson.

2398
02:11:00,208 --> 02:11:01,417
And Grace.

2399
02:11:06,000 --> 02:11:08,083
- (huffs)
- (Jud) Martha.

2400
02:11:08,833 --> 02:11:10,042
Grace.

2401
02:11:12,625 --> 02:11:13,833
You're safe now.

2402
02:11:16,667 --> 02:11:17,875
Let it go.

2403
02:11:19,458 --> 02:11:21,083
Let the hatred go.

2404
02:11:26,458 --> 02:11:27,542
Grace.

2405
02:11:31,208 --> 02:11:32,333
Yes.

2406
02:11:33,208 --> 02:11:34,625
I see it now.

2407
02:11:36,542 --> 02:11:38,167
That poor girl.

2408
02:11:41,333 --> 02:11:43,167
Forgive me, Grace.

2409
02:11:47,375 --> 02:11:48,583
Father…

2410
02:11:51,583 --> 02:11:53,208
You're really good at this.

2411
02:11:53,292 --> 02:11:54,292
(chuckles)

2412
02:11:58,708 --> 02:12:00,875
God, the father of mercies,

2413
02:12:01,625 --> 02:12:04,125
through the death
and resurrection of His Son

2414
02:12:04,208 --> 02:12:06,833
has reconciled the world to Himself

2415
02:12:07,583 --> 02:12:11,750
and poured out the Holy Spirit
for the forgiveness of sins,

2416
02:12:12,583 --> 02:12:14,500
and through the ministry of the Church,

2417
02:12:14,583 --> 02:12:17,000
may God grant you pardon and peace,

2418
02:12:18,000 --> 02:12:20,208
and I absolve you of your sins.

2419
02:12:28,000 --> 02:12:31,208
In the name of the Father and of the Son

2420
02:12:32,292 --> 02:12:33,708
and the Holy Spirit.

2421
02:12:46,167 --> 02:12:47,667
(clangs)

2422
02:12:49,417 --> 02:12:50,500
Shit.

2423
02:13:11,333 --> 02:13:13,125
(Jud breathing heavily)

2424
02:13:15,875 --> 02:13:17,875
(mellow cello music plays)

2425
02:13:20,042 --> 02:13:21,875
(Jud) <i>The jewel was never found.</i>

2426
02:13:26,125 --> 02:13:27,625
<i>The church closed for a while.</i>

2427
02:13:28,542 --> 02:13:31,708
<i>The flock,
what was left of them, scattered.</i>

2428
02:13:32,292 --> 02:13:37,833
<i>Some got what they wanted only to discover
the one thing every holy man knows…</i>

2429
02:13:42,208 --> 02:13:43,833
<i>God has a sense of humor.</i>

2430
02:13:49,375 --> 02:13:51,792
<i>And some got a fresh start.</i>

2431
02:13:52,458 --> 02:13:55,292
<i>Maybe to find a path
that's theirs, I hope so.</i>

2432
02:13:59,042 --> 02:14:00,667
<i>And some got their miracle.</i>

2433
02:14:01,958 --> 02:14:04,375
<i>Not being cured or fixed,</i>

2434
02:14:05,042 --> 02:14:08,125
<i>but finding the sustaining power
to wake up every day</i>

2435
02:14:08,208 --> 02:14:10,333
<i>and do what we're here to do</i>

2436
02:14:11,208 --> 02:14:12,833
<i>in spite of the pain.</i>

2437
02:14:14,000 --> 02:14:15,208
<i>Daily bread.</i>

2438
02:14:18,250 --> 02:14:19,292
